hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Mansur ibn Hayyan narrated to us, who said: Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah narrated to us, who said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib when a man came to him and said: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confide to you? So he became angry and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not confide to me anything he concealed from the people, except that he told me four phrases. He said: So he said: What are they, O Commander of the Believers? He said: He said: Allah has cursed whoever curses his parents, and Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and Allah has cursed whoever shelters an innovator, and Allah has cursed whoever changes the landmarks of the earth."
"602","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me three things, I do not say he forbade the people: wearing a gold ring, and wearing qassi and saffron-dyed saturated garments, and that I recite while bowing or prostrating."
"603","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me three things, I do not say he forbade the people: wearing a gold ring, and wearing qassi and saffron-dyed saturated garments, and that I recite while bowing or prostrating."
"604","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring, and qassi garments, and red velvet saddles."
"605","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa who said: I was sitting with my father, and Ali ibn Abi Talib came to us with a matter of the people's affairs, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Say: O Allah, guide me and set me straight, and remember by guidance Your guiding of the path, and remember by straightness the straightening of the arrowhead against the arrow. And he forbade me to put my ring on this, and Abu Burdah pointed with his thumb toward the index or the middle finger, Asim said: So I was confused which of them it was. He said: And Ali said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the velvet saddle and the qassi garment. He said: As for the velvet saddle, it is something the women used to make for their husbands, placing it upon their saddles. And as for the qassi garment, it is the clothes of Syria, it was said: Syria or Egypt, striped, in which is silk, and in which are figures like citrons. Abu Burdah said: When we saw the sabani garments we knew that it is it."
"606","Zakariyya narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, with his chain, the like of it."
"607","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Azhar ibn Rashid al-Kahili narrated to us, from al-Khidr ibn al-Qawwas al-Bajali, from Abu Sukhaylah, who said: Ali said: Shall I not tell you of the best verse in the Book of Allah, which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us: And whatever misfortune befalls you, it is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much. And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will explain it to you, O Ali: Whatever befalls you of illness, or punishment, or trial in this world is because of what your hands have earned, and Allah is more generous than to repeat the punishment upon you in the Hereafter, and whatever Allah has pardoned in this world, Allah is too majestic to return after His pardon."
"608","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim al-Batin, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who said: We were traveling with Uthman when he heard a man reciting talbiyah for both together. He said: Who is this? They said: Ali. He said: Did you not know that I forbade this? He said: Yes, but I would not abandon the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for your saying."
"609","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: There is none among you except that his seat in Paradise and his seat in Hell have been written. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not then rely? He said: No, act, for each is facilitated. Then he recited: As for he who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best reward, We will facilitate for him the easy way. But as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best reward, We will facilitate for him the difficult way."
"610","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a man from the Ansar over a detachment he sent, and ordered them to listen to him and obey. He said: They angered him about something, so he said: Gather firewood for me. So they gathered, and he said: Kindle a fire. So they kindled it. Then he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not order you to listen to me and obey? They said: Yes. He said: Then enter it. He said: Some of them looked at others and said: We only fled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Fire. He said: So his anger subsided and the fire was extinguished. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they mentioned that to him, and he said: Had they entered it, they would never have come out of it; obedience is only in what is right."
"611","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of its women is Khadijah, and the best of its women is Maryam."
"612","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, who said: I used to think that the soles of the feet are more deserving of wiping than their tops, until I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping their tops."
"613","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Wail, from Abu al-Hayyaj al-Asadi, who said: Ali said: I dispatch you upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched me: That I leave no image except that I efface it, and no grave except that I level it."
"614","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, who said: A man came to Ali and said: I bought a cow. He said: Slaughter it on behalf of seven. He said: Broken-horned. He said: It will not harm you. He said: Lame. He said: When it reaches the place of sacrifice, slaughter it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and the ear closely."
"615","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key of prayer is purification, its prohibition is the takbir, and its release is the taslim."
"616","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rakahs, except Fajr and Asr."
"617","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, who said: Witr is not obligatory like prayer, but it is a sunnah which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established."
"618","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, who said: I saw a man asking forgiveness for his parents while they were both polytheists, so I said: You ask forgiveness for your parents while they are both polytheists? He said: Did Ibrahim not ask forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist? He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was revealed: It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, to the end of the two verses."
"619","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the day of the Trench at an opening of the openings of the Trench, and he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer, until the sun set. May Allah fill their bellies, or: their houses, and their stomachs and their graves with fire."
"620","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, that Ubaydah al-Salmani asked Ali about this, and he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of the hadith of Shubah."
"621","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, who said: We asked Ali about the voluntary prayers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by day, and he said: You cannot bear it. He said: So we said: Tell us of it, we will take from it what we can. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr he waited, until when the sun was from here, meaning from the east, its measure being as that of the Asr prayer from here, meaning from the west, he stood and prayed two rakahs. Then he waited until when the sun was from here, meaning from the east, its measure being as that of the Zuhr prayer from here, meaning from the west, he stood and prayed four, and four before Zuhr when the sun declined, and two after it, and four before Asr, separating between every two rakahs with salutations upon the near angels, the prophets, and those with them of the believers and Muslims. He said: Ali said: Those are sixteen rakahs, the daytime voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and few persist in it."
"622","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the Quran in every state as long as he was not in major impurity."
"623","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Shabi, from Ali, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar came, and he said: These two are the masters of the elderly of the people of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers."
"624","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged the debt before the bequest, while you recite: After any bequest he may have made or debt. And that the full brothers from the same mother inherit to the exclusion of the half-brothers by the father."
"625","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Shubah, who said: Ali ibn Mudrik narrated to me, from Abu Zurah, from Ibn Nujayy, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angel does not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"626","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: Mansur narrated to me, from Ribi, who said: I heard Ali addressing, and he says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."
"627","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Abbad, who said: I and al-Ashtar entered upon Ali, and he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust to you anything he did not entrust to the people in general? He said: No, except what is in this book of mine. He said: So he brought out a book from the sheath of his sword, and in it was: The believers, their blood is equal, and they are one hand against others, and the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf. No believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant during his covenant. Whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"628","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zaidah ibn Qudamah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Let one of you place before him the like of the back of a saddle, then pray."
"629","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: We used to pray while animals passed before us, so we mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The like of the back of a saddle is before one of you, then nothing that passes before him will harm him."
"630","Al-Fadl ibn Sukayn ibn Sukhayt narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: Musa ibn Talhah narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Al-Fadl said: This Sulayman was Kufan, trustworthy."
"631","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from a freedman of Musa ibn Talhah, or from a son of Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution after camel milk and its meat, and would not pray in their resting places, and would not perform ablution after sheep meat and their milk, and would pray in their resting places."
"632","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Nadr, that Uthman ibn Affan called for water for ablution, and with him were al-Zubayr, Talhah, Ali, and Sad, then he performed ablution while they looked on: he washed his face three times, then poured upon his right three times and washed his left three times, and wiped his head, and sprinkled upon his right foot then washed it three times, then sprinkled upon his left foot then washed it three times. Then he said to those present: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution as I have just performed ablution? They said: Yes, and that was because of something that reached him about the ablution of some people."
"633","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Ibrahim, Ibn Dawud said: I think he said: a freedman of ours, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah who said: Three men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will suffice me for these? So I sufficed him for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and a man among them went out and was killed. Then the other two remained with me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and the other went out and was killed. Then the other remained with me, then he fell ill and died on his bed. Talhah said: I saw them in a dream as though the one who died on his bed was the first of them to enter Paradise, and the last of them to enter was the one who was killed first. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What did you find objectionable in this? The believer with so-and-so many tasbihs. Ibn Dawud said: This is its meaning."
"634","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi, from his father who said: We were with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah while we were in ihram, and a bird was gifted to him while Talhah was sleeping. Some of us ate and some refrained. When Talhah woke, he approved of whoever ate, and said: We ate it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"635","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Anas ibn Abi Amir who said: I was with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah when a man entered upon him and said: O Abu Muhammad, we do not know: Is this Yamani more knowledgeable of the Messenger of Allah than you, or is he saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say? He said: By Allah, we do not doubt that he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what we did not hear, and knew what we did not know. We were wealthy people with houses and families, and we used to come to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the two ends of the day, then return. And he was a poor man with no wealth or family; his hand was only with the hand of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to go around with him wherever he went. So we do not doubt that he knew what we did not know and heard what we did not hear. And we have not found anyone with good in him saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. Meaning Abu Hurayrah."
"636","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Khidr ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salma narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Malik ibn Abi Amir, who said: A man came to Talhah ibn Ubaydullah and said: O Abu Muhammad, what do you think of this Yamani, or al-Khidr said: Is the Yamani more knowledgeable of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you, meaning Abu Hurayrah, we hear from him things we do not hear from you? He said: As for his having heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what we did not hear, I have no doubt. And I will tell you about that: We were people of houses, and we only used to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) morning and evening, while he was a poor man with no wealth; he was only at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I have no doubt that he heard what we did not hear. And do you find anyone with good in him saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say?"
"637","Humayd ibn Masadah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Umarah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah and Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hasten the charity of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib by two years."
"638","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: I passed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by people at the tops of palm trees, and he said: What are these doing? They said: They pollinate it, placing the male in the female, so it is pollinated. He said: I do not think that avails anything. They took that and abandoned it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of that, and he said: If it benefits them, let them do it, for I only thought a thought, so do not blame me for opinion. But when I tell you about Allah something, take it, for I will never lie about Allah."
"639","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: I heard Umar saying to Talhah ibn Ubaydullah: Why do I see you disheveled and dusty since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died? Perhaps what is with you is the leadership of your cousin? He said: So he said: Allah forbid. I heard him saying: I know a word none says when death attends him except his soul finds relief with it until it leaves his body, and it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. But I did not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he did not tell me of it. That is what entered me. Umar said: I know it. He said: Praise be to Allah, what is it? He said: The word he said to his uncle. He said: You spoke the truth."
"640","Musa ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Zayd al-Harashi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail who said: I heard al-Shabi, from a man, from Suda wife of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, from Talhah, that he said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a word I did not ask him about until he died, or was taken. He said: I know a word none says at his death except it is a light in his record, and his soul and body find rest with it at death. Umar said: I know it; it is the word he wanted his uncle to say; I see it as nothing but that."
"641","Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad narrated to me, from Misar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talhah, from his mother Suda al-Murriyyah, who said: Umar passed by Talhah after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Why do I see you dejected? Does the leadership of your cousin grieve you? He said: No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know a word none says at his death except it is a light for his record, and his body and soul find relief with it at death. He said: I know it; it is the one he wanted his uncle to say, and had he known anything more saving for him than it, he would have ordered him with it."
"642","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salim al-Makki: That a Bedouin said: I came to Madinah with a milch animal of mine, and I stayed with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, and I said: I have no knowledge of the people of the market, so if only you would sell for me. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a resident to sell for a Bedouin, but go to the market and see who bargains with you, then consult me until I order you or forbid you."
"643","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from a shaykh from Banu Tamim who said: He sat with me while I was in the mosque of Basra in the time of al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, with his staff in his hand and a document he carried in his hand, and he said: O Abdullah, do you see this document benefiting me with this ruler of yours? I said: What is this document? He said: A document the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for us. I said: How did he write it for you? He said: I came to Madinah with my father while I was a young lad with camels we had brought to Madinah to sell them. He said: And Talhah ibn Ubaydullah was a friend of my father. So we stayed with him, and my father said: O Abu Muhammad, go out with us and sell our transport animals for us, for we have no knowledge of this market. He said: As for selling for you, no. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a resident to sell for a Bedouin. But I will go out with you both to the market, and when I approve a man for you among those who trade with you, I will order you to sell to him. He said: So we went out and he went out with us, and he sat in a corner of the market, and men bargained with us for our transport animals, until when a man gave us what satisfied us we came to him and asked his permission about selling to him. He said: Yes, sell to him, for I approve his fidelity and solvency for you. He said: So we sold to him and took what was ours. My father said to him: Get us a document from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that none transgress against us in our charities. He said: That is for every Muslim. So we said: Even so. He said: So he walked with us and said: O Messenger of Allah, these two love that you write for them that none transgress against them in their charities. He said: That is for every Muslim. He said: O Messenger of Allah, they love to have with them a document from you. He said: So he wrote for them this document. So do you see it benefiting me with this ruler of yours? For by Allah, transgression has been committed against us in our charities. He said: I said: By Allah, I do not think so."
"644","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: Talhah ibn Ubaydullah used to say: I do not tell you about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anything, except that I heard him saying: Amr ibn al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abu Abdullah, Umm Abdullah, and Abdullah."
"645","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: Talhah ibn Ubaydullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Amr ibn al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abdullah, Abu Abdullah, and Umm Abdullah."
"646","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: Talhah ibn Ubaydullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Amr ibn al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abdullah, Abu Abdullah, and Umm Abdullah."
"647","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed me, from Abu Salamah, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that two men from Bali accepted Islam, and one of them was killed in the path of Allah, and the other was delayed after the slain one by a year, then died. Talhah said: I saw Paradise in a dream, and I saw the latter of the two men admitted to Paradise before the first. In the morning I narrated that to the people, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Did he not fast Ramadan after him, and pray after him six thousand rakahs, and so-and-so many rakahs?"
"648","Abd al-Ala and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, both said: Al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard my father, Abu Uthman narrated to us, who said: None remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in those days in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fighting except Talhah and Sad. From their hadith."
"649","And several narrated to us, from Mutamir with his chain, the like of it."
"650","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Yahya and Isa sons of Talhah, from their father who said: A camel branded on its face was passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If only the owners of this camel would keep the fire away from this animal? He said: So I said: I will brand in the farthest place from its face. He said: So I branded on the root of the tail."
"651","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you, but how is prayer upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"652","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is prayer upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"653","Abu Musa Harun ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz and others narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Bishr, with his chain, the like of it."
"654","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Zubayd Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Yahya ibn Talhah who said: Umar saw Talhah ibn Ubaydullah grieving, and said: What is with you? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know words none says at death except he is relieved, and his color brightens, and he sees what pleases him. Nothing prevented me from asking him about them except being able to do it. Umar said: I know what they are. Talhah said: What are they? He said: Do you know a word better than a word the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited his uncle to at death? Talhah said: It is by Allah it. Umar said: There is no god but Allah."
"655","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, a shaykh of ours narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a non-muhrim who catches game, may the muhrim eat it? He said: Yes."
"656","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, a shaykh of ours narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a non-muhrim who catches game, may the muhrim eat it? He said: Yes."
"657","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman who said: We went out as pilgrims with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, and game was brought to us; some of us ate and some left it. He rose from his sleep, for he was sleeping, and we told him. He said: Whoever ate did well; we ate it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"658","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from one who narrated to him, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail, one over the other, on the day of Uhud."
"659","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from a man from Banu Tamim called Muadh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail, one over the other, on the day of Uhud."
"660","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sufyan al-Madani narrated to us, Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw the crescent would say: O Allah, bring it upon us with blessing and faith, safety and Islam; my Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"661","Abu Musa Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sufyan narrated to me, who said: I heard Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah narrating from his father, from his grandfather who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the crescent he would say: O Allah, bring it upon us with blessing and faith, safety and Islam; my Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"662","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Musa and Isa sons of Talhah, from their father, that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a Bedouin who came asking him about who fulfilled his vow: Who is he? They did not dare ask him, honoring and revering him. He said: The Bedouin asked him and he turned away from him, then he asked him and he turned away from him. Then I looked out from the door of the mosque wearing green clothes, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: Where is the one asking about who fulfilled his vow? The Bedouin said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is among those who fulfilled their vow."
"663","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him place before him the like of the back of a saddle, then pray and not care who passes beyond that."
"664","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, a shaykh from Banu Zuhrah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is a companion, and my companion is Uthman."
"665","Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim al-Raqashi, from his grandfather Abd al-Malik, from Abu Jarw al-Mazini who said: I witnessed Ali and al-Zubayr when they faced each other, and Ali said to him: O Zubayr, I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You will fight me while you are unjust to me? He said: Yes, and I did not remember except in this stance of mine. Then he left."
"666","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad who said: I heard Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from his father who said: I said to my father al-Zubayr: Why do you not narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as so-and-so and so-and-so narrate from him? He said: I have not parted from him since I accepted Islam, but I heard from him a phrase; I heard him saying: Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"667","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr who said: When this verse was revealed: Indeed you will die and indeed they will die, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will what is between us in this world be repeated upon us along with specific sins? He said: Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every one with a right is given his right."
"668","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid, that a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr narrated to him from al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: envy and hatred, and it is the shaver. I do not say: the shaver of hair, but the shaver of religion. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not tell you of what establishes that for you? Spread peace."
"669","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that day: Talhah made Paradise obligatory when he did for the Messenger of Allah what he did. Ibn Ishaq said: On the day of Uhud the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose toward a rock of the mountain to climb it, and he had become heavy and wore two coats of mail, one over the other. When he went to rise he could not, so Talhah ibn Ubaydullah sat beneath him and he rose until he stood upon it."
"670","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Abdullah ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from his mother and his grandmother Umm Ata, both said: By Allah, it is as if we are looking at al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam when he came to us on a white mule of his, and he said: O Umm Ata, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has forbidden the Muslims to eat the meat of their sacrifices beyond three days, so do not eat it. She said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what do we do with what was gifted to us? He said: What was gifted to you, do with it as you wish."
"671","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: From al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me his parents on the day of Uhud."
"672","Hawtharah ibn Ashras Abu Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, that Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: O my father! I saw you charging on your blond horse on the day of the Trench. He said: Did you see me, O my son? He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day was indeed joining for your father his parents, saying: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"673","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti and Ishaq narrated to us, both said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Bayan, from Wabarah, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father who said: I said to my father al-Zubayr: What prevents you from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as his companions narrate from him? He said: I had a face and station with him, but I heard him saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"674","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to take his ropes, then come to the mountain and bring a bundle of firewood on his back, and sell it and become independent by its price, is better for him than to ask people, whether they give him or withhold."
"675","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr who said: When there was revealed: You will surely be asked that day about pleasure, al-Zubayr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what pleasure are we in, when they are only the two black things? He said: It will surely be."
"676","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to address us and remind us of the days of Allah, until that would be known in his face, as though he were a warner of an army, saying: The matter will come upon you in the morning. He said: And when he had recently been with Gabriel, he would not smile laughing until it was lifted from him."
"677","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Amr ibn Safwan al-Muzani narrated to us, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed us, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning or evening journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."
"678","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Tamim al-Missisi narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar al-Ayli, from Abdullah ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, from his grandmother Umm Ata, freedwoman of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, who said: I heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam saying: When there was revealed: And warn your nearest kin, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out on Abu Qubays: O family of Abd Manaf, I am a warner. Quraysh came to him, and he warned them and frightened them. They said: You claim you are a prophet inspired to, and that to Sulayman were subjected the wind and the mountains, and that to Musa was subjected the sea, and that Isa used to revive the dead? So call Allah to move these mountains from us and to burst the earth for us into rivers, so we take them as plows and sow and eat. Otherwise call Allah to revive our dead so we speak to them and they speak to us. Otherwise call Allah to turn this rock beneath you into gold so we carve from it and it suffices us from the winter and summer journeys. For you claim you are like them. While we were around him, revelation descended upon him, and when it was lifted from him he said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, He has given me what you asked, and had I wished it would be. But He gave me a choice between your entering through the door of mercy so your believer believes, and between leaving you to what you chose for yourselves so you stray from the door of mercy and your believer does not believe. So I chose the door of mercy so your believer believes. And He told me: If He gives you that then you disbelieve, He will punish you with a punishment He punishes none of the worlds with. So there was revealed: And nothing prevented Us from sending the signs except that the former peoples denied them, until he recited three verses, and there was revealed: And if there were a Quran by which the mountains were moved, or the earth cut asunder, or the dead spoken to. The verse."
"679","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would hasten into the thickets, and we would find only the places of our feet."
"680","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kunasah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change gray hair, and do not resemble the Jews."
"681","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, Umm Urwah, as I think, daughter of Jafar ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, narrated to me from her father, from her grandfather al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that he heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for me, for my children, and for the children of my children. He said: I heard my father saying to a sister of mine who was older than me: O my daughter, meaning: That you are among those whom the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached."
"682","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, Umm Urwah narrated to me, from her father, from her grandfather al-Zubayr who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his women in Madinah, he left them in Fari, and among them was Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib, and he left among them Hassan ibn Thabit. A man from the polytheists came to enter upon them, so Safiyyah said to Hassan: The man is yours! Hassan was cowardly and refused her. So Safiyyah took the sword and struck the polytheist with it until she killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of that, and he allotted for Safiyyah a share as he used to allot for men."
"683","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, who said: Umm Urwah narrated to me, from her sister Aishah bint Jafar, from her father, from her grandfather al-Zubayr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he gave him on the day of the conquest of Makkah the banner of Sad ibn Ubadah, so al-Zubayr entered Makkah with two banners."
"684","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hizam ibn Ismail al-Amiri narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Hakim freedman of al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no morning the servants wake except a crier cries: O creatures, glorify the Most Holy."
"685","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, my father al-Zubayr informed me, that when it was the day of Uhud a woman came hurrying until she almost overlooked the slain. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked her seeing them, and said: The woman, the woman. Al-Zubayr said: So I realized she was my mother Safiyyah. He said: So I went out hurrying to her, and I reached her before she ended at the slain. He said: She struck my chest, and she was a strong woman, and said: Away with you, may you have no mother! He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has adjured you. He said: So she stopped and brought out two garments with her, and said: These are two garments I brought for my brother Hamzah. And there beside him was a man from the Ansar slain, with him done as was done with Hamzah. So we found it hard and felt shame that Hamzah be shrouded in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud. So we said: For Hamzah one garment, and for the Ansari one garment. So we measured them, and one was larger than the other, so we cast lots between them, and each of them was placed in the garment that fell to him."
"686","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When there was revealed: Then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection will dispute before your Lord, al-Zubayr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will our dispute in this world be repeated upon us? He said: Yes. He said: I said: Then the matter is surely severe."
"687","Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): One suckling and two sucklings do not prohibit, nor one sip and two sips."
"688","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Rafi, Abu Rafi, narrated to us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Saib who said: Sad ibn Malik came to us after his sight had gone, so I came to him greeting, and I gave him my lineage. He said: Welcome, son of my brother. It reached me that you are good of voice with the Quran. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This Quran descended with sorrow, so when you recite it, weep; if you do not weep, feign weeping, and chant it melodiously. Whoever does not chant it melodiously is not from us."
"689","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Sad, from Sad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the plague: When it occurs while you are in it, do not flee from it. Shubah said: Hisham Abu Bakr narrated to me that he is Ikrimah ibn Khalid."
"690","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Sad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the plague is in a land, do not descend upon it. And when it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."
"691","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Awn who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah who said: Umar said to Sad: They have complained about you in everything, even in prayer. He said: As for me, I prolong the first two and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short of what I followed of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: That is the thought of you, or: That is my thought of you."
"692","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The people of Kufa complained of Sad to Umar, and they said: He does not pray well. Sad said: As for me, I used to pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the two Isha prayers, not omitting from them; I linger in the first two and shorten the last two. Umar said: That is the thought of you, O Abu Ishaq. And he sent men asking about him in Kufa, and they would come to no mosque of the mosques of the people of Kufa except they said good or praised good, until he came to a mosque of the mosques of Banu Abs, and a man called Abu Sadah said: As you have adjured us by Allah, he used not to be just in judgment, nor divide equally, nor march with the detachment. Sad said: O Allah, if he is lying, blind his sight, prolong his life, and expose him to trials. Abd al-Malik said: I saw him afterwards exposing himself to slave girls in the streets, and when asked: How are you? He would say: Old, poor, afflicted; the supplication of Sad befell me."
"693","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir al-Madani narrated to us, who said: Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbid you a little of what intoxicates in large amount."
"694","Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Hudhali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbid you a little of what intoxicates in large amount."
"695","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father who said: My father took a sword from the fifth, and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Grant this to me. But he refused. So Allah revealed: They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger."
"696","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Aidh, from Amir ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that a man came to prayer while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and he said when he reached the row: O Allah, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he said: Who was speaking just now? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then your horse will be hamstrung, and you will be martyred in the path of Allah."
"697","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: I said to Sad ibn Malik: I want to ask you about a hadith, but I fear you to ask you about it. He said: Do not do, O son of my brother; when you know I have knowledge, ask me about it and do not fear me. He said: I said: The saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Ali when he left him in Madinah in the expedition of Tabuk. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you leave me among those who stay behind, among women and children? He said: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So Ali turned away hastening, as if I am looking at the dust of his feet rising. And Hammad said: Ali returned hastening."
"698","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Amir ibn Sad informed me, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I sanctify what is between the two lava plains of Madinah, as Ibrahim sanctified his sanctuary. Its thorn trees are not cut, its game is not killed, and none leaves it desiring other than it except Allah replaces it with better than him. And Madinah is better for them had they known. And none intends them with evil except Allah melts him as lead melts in fire, and as salt melts in water."
"699","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi who said: I told Abu Bakrah, I said: I heard Sad saying: My ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever claims for other than his father in Islam, while he knows he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. He said: And I, my ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"700","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of a man's happiness is his seeking good from his Lord, and his contentment with what He decreed. And part of a servant's wretchedness is his abandoning seeking good, and his anger at what He decreed."
"701","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Wazir Abu al-Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father who said: The servant is ordered to prostrate upon seven bones of his: his face, his hands, his knees, and his feet; whichever he does not place, he has diminished."
"702","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Jafar al-Tahhan narrated to me, Ghassan ibn Bishr al-Kahili narrated to us, from Muslim, from Khaythamah, from Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed the doors of the people into the mosque and opened the door of Ali. People spoke about that, and he said: It is not I who opened it, but Allah opened it."
"703","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Musab ibn Sad who said: I said to my father: O my father, what about His saying: Those who are heedless of their prayer, which of us does not forget? Which of us does not speak to himself? He said: It is not that; it is only wasting the time, amusing himself until the time is lost."
"704","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Simak, from Musab who said: I asked my father Sad and said: O my father: Those who are heedless of their prayer, is it one's forgetfulness in his prayer, the talk of his soul? Sad said: Does not all of us do that? But the one heedless of his prayer is he who prays it outside its time; that is the one heedless of it. Musab said another time: His abandoning prayer at its appointed times."
"705","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq al-Jarmi narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Uthman who said: I told Abu Bakrah, I said: I heard Sad saying: My ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever claims for other than his father in Islam, while he knows he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. He said: And I, my ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"706","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Musab ibn Sad, from Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever supplicates with the supplication of Yunus will be answered."
"707","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Jabir who said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas said to a man: You have no Friday. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why, O Sad? He said: Because he was speaking while you were addressing. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sad spoke the truth."
"708","Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, Shubah said: Before he became confused, who said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: I heard Sad ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ali behind, and he said: Do you leave me behind? He said: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? He said: I am pleased, I am pleased."
"709","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Said ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him from Aishah bint Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from her father, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a woman, and before her were date pits and pebbles with which she glorified Allah. He said: Shall I tell you of what is easier for you than this, or better? Saying: Glory be to Allah as many as what He created in the sky, and glory be to Allah as many as what He created on the earth, and glory be to Allah as many as what is between that, and glory be to Allah as many as what He will create. And Allah is Greater, the like of that. And praise be to Allah, the like of that. And there is no god but Allah, the like of that. And there is no power except with Allah, the like of that."
"710","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Amash mentioning from Abu Ishaq, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every character the believer is imprinted, or he said: folded, upon, Ali ibn Hashim doubted, except treachery and lying."
"711","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Yazid freedman of al-Aswad, that Zayd Abu Ayyash informed him that he asked Sad about white grain, meaning sult, and Sad said: Which of them is better? He said: The white. So he forbade him that. And Sad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about buying dates with fresh dates, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does fresh dates decrease when dry? They said: Yes. So he forbade that."
"712","Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyash, from Sad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"713","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle who said: Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to a group, while Sad was sitting among them. Sad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left one he did not give, while he was the most pleasing of them to me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with you regarding so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. He said: So I was silent a little. Then what I knew of him overcame me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with you regarding so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. He said: So I was silent a little. Then what I knew of him overcame me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with you regarding so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. I give a man while another is more beloved to me than him, fearing he will be thrown into the Fire upon his face."
"714","Zuhayr narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Ibn Abayah, from a freedman of Sad, that Sad saw a son of his praying and supplicating, saying: I ask You for Paradise and its fruits, its bliss, its spouses, and the like of this, at length, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire, its chains, its fetters, its blaze, and the like of this. And Sad was listening. When he finished his prayer, Sad said to him: You asked for a long bliss and sought refuge from a long evil. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be a people who transgress in supplication. And Sad recited: Call upon your Lord humbly and secretly; indeed He does not love the transgressors. He said: I do not know whether he raised it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or it is from the saying of Sad: It suffices you to say: I ask You for Paradise and what brings near to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and what brings near to it of word or deed."
"715","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Musab ibn Sad who said: Sad used to teach us five which he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the worst of age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the world, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave. Shubah said: So I asked Ibn Umayr about the trial of the world, and he said: The Dajjal."
"716","Zuhayr narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats in the morning seven Ajwah dates, no poison or magic will harm him that day. Hashim said: I do not know that Amir mentioned except from the Ajwah of the highlands."
"717","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Malik, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa?"
"718","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father who said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: You have said an evil word. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am new in Islam, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. He said: Say: There is no god but Allah, three times, and spit to your left three times, and seek refuge from Satan, and do not return."
"719","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from his father, raising the hadith, who said: It is not lawful for anyone to boycott his brother beyond three days."
"720","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father who said: I was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him was a leftover of food. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will surely come upon you from this mountain pass a man who eats this leftover, from the people of Paradise. He said: I passed by Umayr ibn Malik while he was performing ablution, and I said to myself: He is its man. We began craning to see the figures of whoever comes upon us. Then Abdullah ibn Salam came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called him to the leftover and he ate it."
"721","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdullah ibn Qays, Abu Khaythamah said: And some of them say: Hakim ibn Abdullah, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father Sad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says when he hears the caller to prayer: And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion, his sin is forgiven."
"722","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani who said: Musab ibn Sad narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Is one of you unable to earn every day a thousand good deeds? He said: A man among his companions asked him: How does one of us earn a thousand good deeds? He said: He glorifies Allah one hundred times, so a thousand good deeds are earned for him, and a thousand evil deeds are removed from him."
"723","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan who said: Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me: That Sad ibn Malik heard a man saying: Labbayk, Owner of the Ascensions. He said: Allah is the Owner of the Ascensions, but we did not used to say that with our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"724","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sad, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet except that he described the Dajjal to his ummah, and I will describe him with a description none before me described: He is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed."
"725","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Muhammad ibn Sad who said: And he used to perform ablution from a waterskin of water. He said: He came out of the privy. He said: So he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. We marveled at that, so we said to him. He said: My father narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing the like of this."
"726","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""A third, and a third is large — or: is much — in bequests."""
"727","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Malik, and Usamah ibn Zayd, and Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The plague is filth and a remnant of the punishment with which a people before you were punished. So if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not enter upon it."""
"728","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I came upon a sword on the day of Badr and it pleased me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me. Then there was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger}."
"729","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from 'Amir, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever you spend on your family of expenditure, you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth."""
"730","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from Sa'd ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of provision is what suffices, and the best of remembrance is the hidden."""
"731","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard Sa'd saying: ""I am indeed the first man among the Arabs to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah, and we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we had no food except acacia leaves and the leaves of the hubalah tree, until one of us would pass stool as a goat passes it, with nothing mixed in it."""
"732","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he gave them, except one man among them. Sa'd said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave them and left so-and-so, while by Allah I consider him a believer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Or a Muslim."" Sa'd said: He said that three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I give a man a gift while another is more beloved to me than him, and I do that only out of fear that Allah will hurl him into the fire of Hell upon his face."""
"733","Zuhayr narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Hakim, 'Amir ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah, so he entered and bowed two rak'ahs in it, then stood and conversed privately with his Lord and left, and said: ""I asked my Lord for three things: He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning nor by famine — meaning hunger — and He gave me both, and I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, and He withheld it from me."""
"734","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: On the day of Badr I came with a sword with me and said: O Messenger of Allah, this sword has healed my breast, so grant it to me. He said: ""This sword belongs neither to you nor to me."" So I left saying: Perhaps he will give it to one whose trial is not like my trial. Then a messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: ""Answer."" So I thought something had been revealed about me because of my words. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You asked me for it while it was not mine, and Allah has now made it mine, so it is yours."""
"735","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""I swore by al-Lat and al-'Uzza, and the covenant is recent."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have spoken an idle evil word. Say: There is no god but Allah, three times, and spit to your left three times, and seek refuge from Satan, and do not repeat it."""
"736","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, that his father Sa'd was among his camels and sheep when his son 'Umar came to him; when he saw him he said: I seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this rider. When he reached him he said: Are you content to be a Bedouin among your camels and sheep while the people in Madinah dispute over kingship? He said: So he struck his chest with his hand and said: O my son, be silent, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah loves the God-fearing, self-sufficient, hidden servant."""
"737","Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided the expedition of Tabuk, he left 'Ali behind in Madinah. So the people said: He was weary of him and disliked his company. That reached 'Ali, so he left until he caught up with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you left me behind in Madinah with the women, children and offspring, until the people said: He was weary of him and disliked his company?"" He said: ""O 'Ali, I have only left you behind over my family. Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"""
"738","Sa'id ibn Mutarrif al-Bahili narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to 'Ali: ""You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet with me."" Sa'id said: So I wanted to hear that directly from Sa'd, so I met him and mentioned to him what 'Amir had mentioned to me, and I said it to him, and he said: Yes, I heard it. I said: Did you hear it yourself? So he put his two fingers into his ears and said: Yes, otherwise let them both become deaf."
"739","Al-Husayn ibn 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Khallad ibn Muslim al-Saffar narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Qays, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, regarding the statement of Allah: {Alif Lam Ra; those are the verses of the clear Book * Indeed We sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you may understand * We relate to you the best of stories} — he said: The Qur'an was sent down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited it to them for a time, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would narrate stories to us? So Allah sent down: {Alif Lam Ra; those are the verses of the clear Book * Indeed We sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an}. So he recited it to them for a time. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would speak to us? So Allah sent down: {Allah sent down the best speech, a consistent Book}. All of that while they are commanded to hold to the Qur'an. My father said: Khallad said: And another besides him added to me in it: They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would remind us? So Allah sent down: {Has the time not come for those who believed that their hearts should become humble at the remembrance of Allah and what has come down of the truth}."
"740","'Ali ibn 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far ibn Najih al-Madini narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu 'Awn narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: 'Umar said to Sa'd: ""The people of Kufah have complained about you in everything, even regarding prayer."" So he said: ""I prolong the first two and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short of what I followed of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" He said: ""That is my expectation of you — or: my opinion of you."""
"741","'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us with something like the hadith of Yahya, except that he said in his hadith: ""That is my expectation of you,"" and he did not doubt."
"742","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard 'Umar saying to Sa'd: ""The people of Kufah have complained about you, to the point that they said: He does not pray well."" He said: Me? He said: Yes. By Allah, I would not fall short with them of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I linger in the first two and shorten the last two. Then I heard 'Umar saying to him: That is my expectation of you; that is my expectation of you."
"743","Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Muhammad, from Bijad ibn Musa, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, he said: Sa'd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes anything of land without right will be collared with it from seven earths; neither supererogatory nor obligatory recompense will be accepted from him. And whoever claims descent from other than his father, or loyalty to other than his patrons, has disbelieved."""
"744","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Fulan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about this verse: {Say: He is Able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It will indeed happen, but its interpretation has not yet come."""
"745","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, he said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said: Concerning me the third was legislated: I fell ill with an illness, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me and said: ""Have you bequeathed?"" I said: I have bequeathed all my wealth. He said: ""Then what have you left for your heirs?"" I said: They are wealthy. He said: ""Bequeath a tenth, and leave the rest for your heirs."" And he mentioned the hadith."
"746","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: ""I fell ill in the year of the Conquest with an illness in which I came close to death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me visiting me in it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and none inherits from me except my daughter; shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: 'No.' I said: Then half? He said: 'No.' I said: Then a third? He said: 'A third, and a third is large — or: is much. That you leave your heirs wealthy is better than leaving them dependent begging from people. You will not spend any expenditure but you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind from my emigration? He said: 'You will not be left behind after me and do a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will increase in rank and degree, and perhaps you will be left behind so that some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their emigration, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah,' expressing sorrow for him that he died in Makkah."""
"747","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an."" Sufyan said: Meaning: find sufficiency in it."
"748","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sharik ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Namir — and he is one of Banu al-Harith ibn 'Abd Manah ibn Kinanah — 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas informed me, that his father, when he saw the disagreement of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and their dispersal, bought livestock for himself, then left and secluded himself with it with his family at a water called Qalahhi. He said: And Sa'd was among the sharpest of people in eyesight, so one day he saw something moving and said to those following him: Do you see anything? They said: We see something like a bird. He said: I see a rider upon a camel. Then after a short while 'Umar ibn Sa'd came upon a Bactrian camel. Then he said: O Allah, we seek refuge in You from the evil of what he has brought. Then 'Umar greeted, then said to his father: Are you content to follow the tails of this livestock among these mountains while your companions dispute over the affair of the ummah? So Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""There will be trials after me — or he said: matters — the best of people in them is the wealthy, hidden, God-fearing one. So if you can, O my son, to be like that, then be so."" Then 'Umar said to him: Is there nothing else with you? So Sa'd said to him: No, O my son. So 'Umar leapt to ride, and he had not dismounted from his camel. So Sa'd said to him: Wait until we give you lunch. He said: I have no need of your lunch. Sa'd said: Then we will milk for you and give you drink. He said: I have no need of your drink. Then he rode and left on the spot."
"749","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from 'Ayyash ibn 'Abbas, from Bukayr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said at the time of the turmoil of 'Uthman: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will be a trial: the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening."" He said: What if he enters upon me in my house and stretches his hand to kill me? He said: ""Be like the son of Adam."""
"750","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: ""Concerning me the prohibition of wine was revealed: I drank with a group of the Ansar before it was prohibited, and a man among them struck me on my nose with the jawbone of a camel. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the prohibition of wine was revealed."""
"751","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Sa'd said: ""I am indeed the first man to shoot an arrow at the polytheists, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never joined both his parents together for anyone before me, and I heard him saying: 'Shoot, O Sa'd; may my father and mother be your ransom.'"""
"752","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, al-'Ala' ibn Abi al-'Abbas narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl narrating from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd ibn Malik, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned, meaning Dhu al-Thudayyah, who was found with the people of al-Nahr — so he said: ""A devil of Radhah; a man of Bajilah will bring him down, called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, a mark among an unjust people."" Sufyan said: So 'Ammar al-Duhni said when he narrated: A man of ours, of Bajilah, brought him and said: I think he is so-and-so of Duhn, called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab."
"753","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl and ate from it, and a leftover remained. So he said: ""A man of the people of Paradise will come from this mountain pass and eat this leftover."" Sa'd said: And I had left my brother 'Umayr performing ablution, so I said: It is 'Umayr. He said: Then 'Abdullah ibn Salam came and ate it."
"754","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to 'Ali: ""You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."" Sa'id said: So I wanted to hear that directly from Sa'd, so I met him and mentioned to him what 'Amir had mentioned to me, and he said: Yes, I heard it. I said: Did you hear it yourself? So he put his two fingers into his ears and said: ""Yes, otherwise let them both become deaf."""
"755","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Sakhr informed me, that Abu Hazim narrated to him from Ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Faith began as strange and will return as it began. So glad tidings to the strangers on that day, when people have become corrupt. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Islam will surely contract between these two mosques as a snake contracts into its hole."""
"756","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: al-Suddi claimed, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to the people except four men and two women, and said: ""Kill them, even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah: 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, 'Abdullah ibn Khatal, Miqyas ibn Subabah, and 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi al-Sarh."" As for 'Abdullah ibn Khatal, he was caught while clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah, and Sa'id ibn Hurayth and 'Ammar ibn Yasir raced to him; Sa'id outran 'Ammar — and he was the younger of the two men — and killed him. As for Miqyas ibn Subabah, the people caught him in the market. As for 'Ikrimah, he boarded the sea and a storm struck them, so the ship's crew said to the people of the ship: Be sincere, for your gods avail you nothing here. So 'Ikrimah said: If nothing but sincerity will save me at sea, then nothing but it will save me on land. O Allah, I make a covenant to You: if You spare me from what I am in, I will come to Muhammad until I place my hand in his hand, and I will surely find him pardoning and generous. He said: So he came and accepted Islam. As for 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi al-Sarh, he hid with 'Uthman ibn 'Affan; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to allegiance, he brought him until he stood him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept the allegiance of 'Abdullah. So he raised his head and looked at him three times, each time refusing; then he accepted his allegiance after the third. Then he turned to his Companions and said: ""Was there not among you a resolute man to stand to this man — when he saw me withholding my hand from his allegiance — and kill him?"" They said: How would we know, O Messenger of Allah, what was in your mind?"" He said: ""It is not fitting for a prophet to have treacherous glances."""
"757","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Malik, from Sa'd ibn Malik, that he proposed to a woman in Makkah while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: ""Would that I had someone with me who sees her and informs me about her."" Then a man called Hit said: I will describe her to you: when she comes forward you say: she walks upon six, and when she turns away you say: she walks upon four. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""I see this one as objectionable; I think he knows women's matters."" And he used to enter upon Sawdah, so he forbade him from entering upon her. When he arrived in Madinah he banished him, and he remained so until the rule of 'Umar; then he exerted himself, and he would permit him to enter Madinah on Friday, and charity would be given to him."
"758","'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, he said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas led us in prayer and stood up during the two rak'ahs, so we glorified Allah for him, but he stood fully upright. He said: So he continued in his standing until he finished, then said: ""Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."" Abu 'Uthman 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid said: We have not heard anyone raising this except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"759","'Amr narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Sa'd ibn Malik led us in prayer, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah, but he did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"760","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The greatest of Muslims in crime against Muslims is one who asked about a matter that had not been forbidden to people, and it was then forbidden to people because of his question."""
"761","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The greatest of Muslims in crime is one who asked about a matter that had not been forbidden to people, and it was then forbidden because of his question."""
"762","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something like it."
"763","Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: I remember as I remember 'In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,' from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The greatest of Muslims among Muslims in crime is one who asks about a matter that had not been forbidden to people, and it was then forbidden because of his question."""
"764","'Abdullah ibn Muti' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: When Ziyad claimed lineage, I met Abu Bakrah. He said: So I said: What is this that you have done? He said: I heard Sa'd narrating, saying: My two ears heard and my heart retained the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever claims descent in Islam to a father while he knows he is not his father, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him."" Then Abu Bakrah said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"765","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq narrated to him that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated from the hadith of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""No hamah, no contagion, and no omen; and if there is anything in birds, then it is in the woman, the horse and the house."" And he used to say: ""If the plague is in a land, do not descend upon it, and if it is in a land while you are in it, do not flee from it."""
"766","Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, he said: Abu Mushir narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of 'Umar ibn 'Ubaydillah, narrated to me, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: ""I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying of anyone: He is of the people of Paradise, except for 'Abdullah ibn Salam."""
"767","Abu Salih Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa al-Juhani narrated to me, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, teach me words to say. He said: ""Say: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; Allah is Most Great, greatly; and praise be to Allah abundantly; and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; there is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Mighty, the Wise."" He said: These are for my Lord; so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, and grant me well-being."""
"768","Mus'ab ibn 'Abdillah al-Zubayri narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Ibn 'A'idh, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, he said: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading us in prayer, and said: O Allah, grant me the best of what You grant the righteous. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: ""Who was speaking just now?"" The man said: I was. He said: Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be killed in the path of Allah."""
"769","Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Qanan ibn 'Abdillah al-Nahmi narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us, from his father, he said: I was sitting in the mosque, I and two men with me, and we spoke ill of 'Ali. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came angrily, anger recognizable in his face, so I sought refuge with Allah from his anger. Then he said: ""What is with you and with me? Whoever harms 'Ali has harmed me — the hadith."""
"770","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us these words: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the most feeble age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the world and the punishment of the grave."""
"771","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Sa'd, he said: I passed by 'Uthman ibn 'Affan in the mosque and greeted him; he stared at me, then did not return the greeting. So I came to the Commander of the Believers 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Believers, has anything new happened in Islam? He said: What is it? I said: Nothing, except that I passed by 'Uthman just now in the mosque and greeted him; he stared at me, then did not return the greeting. He said: So 'Umar sent to 'Uthman and called him, and said: What prevents you from having returned your brother's greeting? 'Uthman said: I did not do that. Sa'd said: I said: Yes, you did. He said: Until he swore and I swore. He said: Then 'Uthman remembered and said: Yes. I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. You passed by me just now while I was speaking to myself about a word I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, I never remember it except that a covering comes over my sight and heart. Then Sa'd said: So I will inform you of it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to us the first supplication, then a Bedouin came and distracted him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and I followed him. When I feared he would reach his house before me, I struck the ground with my foot, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to me and said: ""Who is this — Abu Ishaq?"" He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""What is it?"" He said: I said: Nothing, by Allah, except that you mentioned to us the first supplication, then this Bedouin came. Then he said: Yes — the supplication of Dhu al-Nun: {There is no god but You; glory be to You; indeed I have been of the wrongdoers}. For no Muslim ever supplicates his Lord with it for anything but He answers him."""
"772","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Mu'adh al-Taymi, he said: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Two prayers after which there is no prayer: the dawn prayer until the sun rises, and the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."""
"773","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Abu 'Abdillah al-Qarraẓ, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."""
"774","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan ibn al-'Ala' ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam Abu al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will humiliate him."""
"775","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard my father saying: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying of a living, walking person: He is of the people of Paradise, except for 'Abdullah ibn Salam."
"776","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shaqiq ibn Abi 'Abdillah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Khalid ibn 'Urfutah, that he came to Sa'd ibn Malik and said: It has reached me that you are being pressed to revile 'Ali in Kufah — have you reviled him? He said: Allah forbid. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Sa'd, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about 'Ali something such that if a saw were placed on my parting to make me revile him, I would never revile him."
"777","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I give a man while another is more beloved to me than him, out of fear that he will topple upon his face into the Fire."""
"778","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'd ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me while I was ill and said: ""Have you bequeathed?"" I said: Yes. He said: By how much? I said: With all my wealth in the path of Allah. He said: Then what have you left for your child? He said: I said: They are wealthy with goodness. He said: Bequeath a tenth. I kept decreasing and he kept decreasing with me until he said: ""Bequeath a third, and a third is much."" Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: So we prefer that less than a third be bequeathed, because of the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""And a third is much."""
"779","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from a man of Banu 'Amir, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I fear for you the trial of prosperity more than the trial of adversity. You have been tested with the trial of adversity and you were patient; and indeed the world is green and sweet."""
"780","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from 'Amr ibn Sa'id, he said: We were with Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman in the slave market; he left us, then returned to us and said: This is the last of three men of Banu Sa'd, all of whom narrated to me this hadith. He said: Sa'd fell ill in Makkah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him visiting him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I fear dying in the land as Sa'd ibn Khawlah died, so supplicate to Allah to heal me. So he said: ""O Allah, heal Sa'd"" — three times. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and I have no heir except distant kindred; shall I bequeath half my wealth? He said: ""No."" He said: Then shall I bequeath a third of my wealth? He said: A third is large — or: is much. Your charity from your wealth is charity for you, and your wife's eating from your food is charity, and your spending on your family is charity, and that you leave your family after you living — or he said: wealthy — is better than that they beg."""
"781","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father, that some verses of the Qur'an were revealed concerning him. He said: Sa'd's mother swore she would never speak to him until he disbelieved in his religion, and would neither eat nor drink. She said: You claim that Allah enjoined upon you kindness to parents, and I am your mother, and I command you with this. He said: She remained three days until she fainted from exhaustion; then a son of hers called 'Umarah stood and gave her drink, and she began supplicating against Sa'd. So Allah sent down this verse: {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents * but if they strive with you to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them; to Me is your return and I will inform you of what you used to do}. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gained a great spoil, and in it was a sword. So I took it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Grant me this sword as extra booty, for I am one whose standing you know. He said: So he said: ""Return it to where you took it from."" So I went back with it, then I returned after that and asked him again, and he said: ""Return it to where you took it from."" So I set out until, when I was about to throw it into the collected spoils, my soul reproached me, so I returned to him and said: Give it to me. He said: So he raised his voice to me and said: ""Return it to where you took it from."" Then Allah sent down: {They ask you about the spoils}. And I sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to me, and I said: Let me distribute my wealth wherever I wish. He refused; so I said: Then half. He refused; so I said: Then a third. He remained silent. So a third was considered permissible. He said: And I came upon a group of the Ansar and the Muhajirun, and they said: Come, we will feed you and give you wine to drink — and that was before wine was prohibited. So I came to them in a garden — and the hashsh is a garden — and there was a roasted camel's head with them and a skin of wine. He said: So I ate and drank with them. He said: Then I mentioned the Ansar and the Muhajirun, and I said: The Muhajirun are better than the Ansar. He said: So a man took the jawbone of the head and struck me with it, wounding my nose. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and Allah sent down concerning me — meaning himself — the matter of wine: {Wine, gambling, idols and divining arrows are but filth from the work of Satan}."
"782","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of the West will remain manifest upon the truth until the Hour comes."""
"783","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-'Ala' ibn Abi al-'Abbas, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned Dhu al-Thudayyah. He said: ""A devil of Radhah; a man of Bajilah will bring him down, called al-Ashhab — or Ibn al-Ashhab — a mark among an unjust people."""
"784","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd, that he stood up during the two rak'ahs and they glorified Allah for him. He said: So he stood fully upright. He said: And he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he finished, then said: Do you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"785","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Umarah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar, 'Amir ibn Sa'd informed me, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""No man takes seven dates in the morning from between its two lava plains but poison will harm him that day."""
"786","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes seven 'Ajwah dates in the morning, neither poison nor magic will harm him that day."""
"787","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Sa'd saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused 'Uthman ibn Maẓ'un celibacy, and had he permitted him, we would have castrated ourselves."
"788","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu 'Uthman, from Sa'd ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be a trial: the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening, and the one hastening in it is better than the one riding, and the one riding in it is better than the one urging on."""
"789","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Iyas, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah is Good and loves what is good, Clean and loves cleanliness, Generous and loves generosity, Munificent and loves munificence. So clean your houses, and do not resemble the Jews who gather rubbish in their houses."""
"790","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi, narrated to us, Khalid ibn Iyas al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hassan, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: ""Allah is Good and loves what is good, Clean and loves cleanliness, Generous and loves generosity, Munificent and loves munificence. So clean your courtyards and open spaces, and do not resemble the Jews who gather rubbish in their houses."" Khalid said: So I mentioned that to Muhajir ibn Mismar, and he said: 'Amir ibn Sa'd narrated it to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — except that he said: ""Clean your courtyards."""
"791","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Malik ibn al-Harith — al-A'mash said: And I heard them mentioning it from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, and I do not know them but that they mentioned it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Deliberation in everything is good, except in the deeds of the Hereafter."""
"792","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was supplicating with two fingers, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Make it one, make it one,"" and pointed with the forefinger."
"793","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas stood up during the two rak'ahs, so they glorified Allah for him and he stood fully. Then he said: ""Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."""
"794","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: I heard Sa'd saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined both his parents together for me on the day of Uhud. Yahya said: I think he said: ""May my father and mother be your ransom."" And Sa'd was a skilled archer."
"795","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Musa al-Juhani informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me words to say. He said: ""Say: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; Allah is Most Great, greatly; and praise be to Allah abundantly; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; there is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Mighty, the Wise."" He said: This is for my Lord; so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me."""
"796","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""That the belly of one of you be filled with pus until it overflows is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."""
"797","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastawa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hadrami, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I asked Sa'd about omens and he rebuked me, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""No contagion and no omen; and if omens are in anything, then they are in the horse, the woman and the house."""
"798","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The hand is cut for the price of a shield."""
"799","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Salim ibn Hayyan, 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Sa'd narrated to him, from his father, he said: The plague was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""A filth with which those before you were afflicted; so if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if it is in it, do not enter it."""
"800","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, and Abu Sa'id the freedman of Banu Hashim, from 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to greet to his right until his cheek was visible, and to his left until his cheek was visible."""
"801","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: ""'Uthman sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for celibacy, and had he permitted him, we would have castrated ourselves."""
"802","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him visiting him while he was in Makkah, and he disliked dying in the land from which he had emigrated. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on Sa'd ibn 'Afra'."" And he had only one daughter. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: ""No."" He said: Then half? He said: No. He said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much. That you leave your heirs wealthy is better than leaving them dependent begging with their hands. Whatever expenditure you spend, it is charity — even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. And perhaps Allah will provide for you, so that some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you."""
"803","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu 'Abdillah al-Qarraẓ narrated to us, that he heard Sa'd ibn Malik and Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their city, and bless them in their sa' and bless them in their mudd. O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and intimate friend, and I am Your servant and Messenger; and Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and I ask You for the people of Madinah the like of what Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and the like of it with it. Madinah is latticed: over every mountain pass of it are two angels guarding it; neither plague nor the Dajjal enters it. Whoever intends it with evil, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."""
"804","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Nawfal: that he heard Sa'd ibn Malik and al-Dahhak ibn Qays, in the year Mu'awiyah performed Hajj, while they were discussing tamattu' with 'Umrah to Hajj. Al-Dahhak said: ""None does that except one ignorant of Allah's command."" Then Sa'd said: ""Evil is what you have said, O son of my brother."" Al-Dahhak said: ""'Umar forbade it."" Then Sa'd said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it, and we did it with him."""
"805","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Ya'la, from Sulayman ibn Abi 'Abdillah, he said: I witnessed Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas when some people came to him concerning a servant of theirs whose spoil Sa'd had taken: he saw him hunting in the sanctuary of Madinah which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had declared sacred, so he took his spoil. They spoke to him to return their spoil, but he refused and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he demarcated the boundaries of the sanctuary of Madinah: ""Whomever you catch hunting within these boundaries, whoever catches him, his spoil belongs to him."" So I will not return to you a morsel with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed me; but if you wish, I will compensate you the price of his spoil."
"806","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The month is like this and like this and like this: ten and ten, and nine once."""
"807","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi 'Atiq narrated to me, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""If one of you spits while he is in the mosque, let him conceal his phlegm, lest it touch the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him."""
"808","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to 'Ali this statement: ""Will you not be pleased, O 'Ali, to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"""
"809","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd narrated to me, that Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to him from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: 'Umar sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there were women of Quraysh with him, speaking to him and asking much of him, their voices raised. When he sought permission, they stood hastening to the veil. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him permission while laughing. 'Umar said: May Allah make your tooth laugh, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I marvelled at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they hastened to the veil."" 'Umar said: Then it is you, O Messenger of Allah, whom they should have feared more. Then 'Umar said: O enemies of yourselves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes; you are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Satan never meets you travelling a mountain pass but that he travels a pass other than yours."""
"810","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Muhammad ibn 'Ikrimah, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that the owners of farms in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lease their farms for what grows along the water channels of the crop, and what is watered around the well. So they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and disputed about some of that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them from leasing for that, and said to them: ""Lease for gold and silver."""
"811","Zahmwayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, he said: ""I prayed and joined my fingers together between my knees, and my father forbade me, and said: We were commanded to place our hands upon the knees."""
"812","'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghayyab, Abu Bahr, narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: {Alif Lam Mim * The revelation}, and {Has there come upon man}."
"813","'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it."" He said: And he took my hand and seated me in this seat of mine to teach recitation."
"814","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Umm 'Abdillah bint Nabil, the freedwoman of 'A'ishah bint Sa'd, narrated to me, from 'A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father Sa'd, he said: ""I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he found a fallen date cluster containing dates; so he took a date and gave me a date."""
"815","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better than that it be filled with poetry."""
"816","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim also narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Jubayr narrating from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."""
"817","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Abu al-Zinad, from 'A'ishah bint Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the road of al-Far' he would enter ihram when his mount stood upright with him; and when he took the other road, he would enter ihram when he ascended the height of al-Bayda'."""
"818","Several narrated it to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah and others. They said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, with its chain, something like it."
"819","Muhammad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abu Suhayl ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Baqi' al-Khayl when al-'Abbas came forward. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin."""
"820","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hand me arrows on the day of Uhud, saying: ""Shoot; may my father and mother be your ransom."""
"821","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about {Those who are heedless of their prayer}. He said: ""They are those who delay prayer beyond its time."""
"822","Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The month is like this, and like this, and like this,"" then he decreased a finger on the third."
"823","Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If one of you spits in the mosque, let him bury it, lest it touch the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him."""
"824","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu 'Ayyash, that Sa'd was asked about white wheat for barley and disliked it, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about fresh dates for dry dates, and he said: ""Does the fresh date decrease when it dries?"" They said: Yes. He said: ""Then no."""
"825","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Sa'd: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening}. He said: It was revealed concerning six: I and Ibn Mas'ud are among them; and the polytheists had said to him: Would you keep these close?"
"826","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Nawfal informed me, that he heard al-Dahhak ibn Qays, during the Hajj of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, saying: None gives a verdict for tamattu' with 'Umrah to Hajj except one ignorant of Allah's command. Then Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said to him: ""Evil is what you have said, O son of my brother; by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that, and we did it with him."""
"827","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim al-Sa'igh, from a steward of Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever withholds surplus water, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"828","Al-Mu'alla narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?"" A man among his companions said to him: How would a thousand good deeds be written for him? He said: ""He glorifies Allah a thousand times, so a thousand good deeds are written for him, and a thousand sins are erased from him."""
"829","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried? He said: ""The prophets, then the most exemplary, then the most exemplary; a servant is tried according to his religion."" He said: ""Tribulation keeps afflicting the servant until he walks upon the earth with no sin upon him."" Hammad said: 'Asim shook it."
"830","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Kill the little corrupt one — meaning the gecko."""
"831","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it."
"832","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Ikrimah, from Sa'd ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him on the day of Uhud while he was shooting: ""Bravo; may my father and mother be your ransom."""
"833","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me visiting me in the year of the Farewell Hajj because of a pain that had become severe upon me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the pain has reached me as you see, and I am wealthy, and none inherits from me except a daughter of mine; shall I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity? He said: No. I said: Then half of it? He said: ""No."" Then he said: A third, and a third is large — or much. That you leave your heirs wealthy is better for you than leaving them dependent begging from people. And you will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will be rewarded for it — even what you place in your wife's mouth. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my companions? He said: ""You will not be left behind and do a righteous deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will increase thereby in degree and rank; and perhaps you will be left behind so that some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their emigration and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah,"" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressing sorrow for him, in the year he died in Makkah."
"834","From the Musnad of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf. Zuhayr narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ten in Paradise: Abu Bakr in Paradise, 'Umar in Paradise, 'Uthman in Paradise, 'Ali in Paradise, Talhah in Paradise, al-Zubayr in Paradise, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf in Paradise, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas in Paradise, Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn 'Amr in Paradise, and Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah in Paradise."""
"835","Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrami narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Awn, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: I said to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf: O uncle, inform me of your story on the day of Badr. He said: Read after one hundred and twenty of Al 'Imran and you will find our story: {When you left your family in the morning to station the believers for battle} up to His statement: {When two parties among you were about to lose heart}. He said: They are those who sought protection from the polytheists — up to His statement: {And you had wished for death before meeting it; now you have seen it while you look on}. He said: So it is the wishing to meet the believers — up to His statement: {When you were slaying them by His permission}."
"836","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to Syria until, when he was at Sargh, the commanders of the armies met him: Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and his companions. They informed him that an epidemic had fallen upon Syria. 'Umar said: Call the first Muhajirun for me. So they were called for him, and he consulted them. Some of them said: You went out for a purpose and we do not think you should return. And some of them said: With you are the rest of the people and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not think you should advance them upon this epidemic. So he said to them: Withdraw from me. Then he said: Call the Ansar for me. So they were called for him, and he consulted them, and they followed the way of the Muhajirun and differed as they differed. He said: Stand away from me. Then he said: Call for me whoever is here of the elders of Quraysh, of the Muhajirun of the Conquest. So they were called for him, and he consulted them, and not two men disagreed with him. They said: We think you should return with the people and not advance them upon this epidemic. So 'Umar called out: I am departing in the morning on my mount; so gather to me. Then Abu 'Ubaydah said: Fleeing from the decree of Allah? He said: If only someone other than you had said it, O Abu 'Ubaydah. Yes — fleeing from the decree of Allah to the decree of Allah. Tell me: if you had camels and descended into a valley with two sides, one fertile and the other barren — is it not that if you pasture the fertile one you pasture it by Allah's decree, and if you pasture the barren one you pasture it by Allah's decree? Then 'Abd al-Rahman came — and he had been absent attending to some need of his — and said: I have knowledge of this: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""If you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it."" So 'Umar praised Allah and then departed."
"837","Zuhayr narrated to us, Bishr ibn 'Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab adjured a group among whom was 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf: I adjure you by Allah, by Whose permission the heaven and earth stand — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity?"" They said: Yes."
"838","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Makhul narrated to me, from Kurayb the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, he said: I sat with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said to me: O Ibn 'Abbas, have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding the Muslim man when he forgets in his prayer, what he should do? He said: So I said: No, by Allah; and have you heard, O Commander of the Believers, anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? He said: So he said: No, by Allah. While we were in that, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf came and said: What are you two discussing? He said: So 'Umar said to him: I asked him, and informed him of what he had asked him. Then 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: But I have heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding about that. Then 'Umar said to him: Then you are trustworthy with us; so what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: So 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""If one of you forgets in his prayer so that he does not know whether he added or decreased — if he doubts between one and two, let him count it as one; and if he doubts between two and three, let him count it as two; and if he doubts between three and four, let him count it as three, until the doubt is in addition. Then let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting before greeting, then greet."""
"839","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, that Abu al-Raddad complained of illness, and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf visited him and said: The best of them and most joining of kin is Abu Muhammad. Then 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah said: I am Allah, and I am al-Rahman, and it is the womb-tie; I created the womb-tie and derived for it a name from My Name. So whoever joins it, I join him; and whoever severs it, I sever him — or: cut him off."""
"840","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawa'i informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah ibn Qariz, that his father narrated to him: that he visited 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf while visiting the sick, and 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: May kinship join you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah said: I am al-Rahman and it is the womb-tie; I split for it a name from My Name. So whoever joins it, I join him; and whoever severs it, I sever him — or he said: cut him off, I cut him off."""
"841","Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydillah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, he said: I saw 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf circumambulating the House while chanting, wearing leather socks. 'Umar said to him: ""I do not know which is more astonishing: your chanting around the House, or your circumambulating in your socks?"" He said: ""I did this in the time of one better than you: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he did not find fault with it in me."""
"842","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydillah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf circumambulating the House while chanting, wearing leather socks. He said: By Allah, I do not know whether your circumambulating in your socks is more astonishing, or your chanting around the House? He said: I did that in the time of one better than you: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"843","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I witnessed, as a boy, an alliance with my uncles, of the Mutayyabun; I would not wish to break it even for red camels."""
"844","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I witnessed as a boy, with my uncles, the alliance of the Mutayyabun; I would not wish to break it even for red camels."""
"845","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I witnessed with my uncles..."" and he mentioned something like it."
"846","Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Uthman, from Ibn Abi Sandar al-Aslami, from a freedman of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman said: I was standing in the courtyard of the mosque when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming out of the door next to the graveyard. I waited a while, then went out after him, and found him having entered a garden of the Asawif. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, then prostrated a prostration and prolonged the prostration in it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the tashahhud, I hastened toward him and said: May my father and mother be your ransom; you prostrated a prostration so long that I feared Allah had taken your soul. He said: ""Jibril gave me glad tidings that whoever sends blessings upon me, Allah sends blessings upon him; and whoever greets me with peace, Allah grants him peace."""
"847","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, when he went out to Syria and heard of the plague, held back from that. 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""If you hear that it has fallen upon a land, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave fleeing from it."" So 'Umar returned on account of the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf."
"848","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami and Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us; they said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: The judge of the people of Palestine narrated to me, he said: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things — by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I would indeed swear upon them: no wealth decreases from charity, so give charity; and no man pardons a wrong seeking thereby the Face of Allah but Allah raises him thereby in honour on the Day of Resurrection; and no man opens for himself a door of begging but Allah opens for him a door of poverty."""
"849","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from the judge of the people of Palestine, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and he mentioned something like it."
"850","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Affan al-Ghatafani narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Kharrabudh narrated to us, from an elder of the people of Madinah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turbaned me, letting its ends hang in front of me and behind me."
"851","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kurayb al-Hamdani narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd ibn Sa'id ibn Nufayl narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Mus'ab, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The adornment of the world will be lifted in the year one hundred and twenty-five."""
"852","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that he witnessed that when 'Uthman ibn 'Affan gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that with which he equipped the army of hardship, bringing seven hundred uqiyyahs of gold."
"853","Al-Hasan ibn Isma'il Abu Sa'id al-Basri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf while he was leading the people in prayer, 'Abd al-Rahman wanted to step back, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signalled to him: ""Stay in your place."" So he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the prayer of 'Abd al-Rahman."
"854","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Humayd ibn Abi 'Abdillah, from Abu Salamah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I saw him prostrating in {When the sky splits open} ten times."""
"855","Al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma' al-Jarmi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: He and 'Umar discussed prayer together. He said: Then 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf passed by us and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Saying: ""So I bear witness with Allah's testimony that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If one of you prays and is in doubt about deficiency in his prayer, let him pray until he is in doubt about excess."""
"856","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Abdillah al-Rumi narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Khalil ibn Murrah narrating from Mubashshir, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The scholar is favoured over the worshipper by seventy degrees; between every two degrees is as between heaven and earth."""
"857","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Zayd ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out seeking a man of the Ansar and called him. The Ansari came out of his house to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his head dripping water. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is with your head?"" He said: You called me while I was with my wife, so I feared being delayed from you; so I hastened, stood, poured water over myself, then came out. He said: Had you ejaculated? He said: No. He said: If you do that, then do not wash fully; wash what touched the woman of you, and perform your ablution for prayer — for water is only from water."
"858","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, Qays ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather 'Abd al-Rahman, he said: Five or four of us among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what befell him of needs by night and day. He said: So I came to him after he had gone out, and followed him; he entered a garden of the gardens of the Asawif, prayed, and prostrated, prolonging the prostration. I said: Allah has taken his soul. He said: So he raised his head and called me, and said: What is with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the prostration; I said: Allah has taken the soul of His Messenger; I shall never see him again. He said: I prostrated in gratitude to my Lord for what He has bestowed upon me regarding my ummah: whoever of my ummah sends one blessing upon me, ten good deeds are written for him, and ten evil deeds are erased from him."
"859","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Talhah, from al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdillah, from Mus'ab ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, he turned to Ta'if and besieged it nineteen or eighteen days without conquering it. Then he travelled on in the late afternoon or early morning, then alighted, then set out at midday and said: ""O people, I am your forerunner, and I enjoin upon you good regarding my kin; and your appointment is the Pool. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they shall establish prayer and give zakah — or I shall surely send to them a man from me — or: like myself — and he shall strike the necks of their fighters and take captive their offspring."" He said: So the people thought it was Abu Bakr or 'Umar. Then he took the hand of 'Ali and said: ""This is he."""
"860","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr, Bajalah heard, he said: I was a scribe for Jaz' ibn Mu'awiyah, the uncle of al-Ahnaf, when the letter of 'Umar came to us a year before his death, saying: Kill every sorcerer, separate every Magian from his close kin, and forbid them humming. So we killed three sorceresses, and we began separating a man from his kinswoman according to the Book of Allah; and he prepared much food and invited the Magians, laying the sword upon his thigh; and they cast down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and ate without humming. And 'Umar had not taken jizyah from the Magians until 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"861","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Bajalah narrating to Abu al-Sha'tha' and 'Amr ibn Aws, in the year Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr performed Hajj, while he was beside the steps of Zamzam: I was a scribe for Jaz' ibn Mu'awiyah, the uncle of al-Ahnaf, when 'Umar's order came to him a year before his death: Kill every sorcerer, separate every Magian from his close kin, and forbid them humming. He said: So we killed three sorceresses, and we began separating a woman from her kin according to the Book of Allah; and he prepared much food, invited the Magians and laid the sword upon his thigh; so they cast down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and ate without humming. He said: And 'Umar had not taken jizyah from the Magians until 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"862","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: What shall I do regarding the Magians? He said: So 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf stood and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he was asked about them — saying: ""Their practice is the practice of the People of the Book."""
"863","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward emerges from his sins as on the day his mother bore him."""
"864","Hudbah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: I was at 'Arafat when I met Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. I said: Narrate to me something you heard from your father, with no one between your father and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: My father narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah has obligated the fast of Ramadan, and I have established its standing in prayer."""
"865","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, my father informed me, my father narrated to me, from al-Nadr ibn Shayban, he said: I said to Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: Will you not narrate to us a hadith you heard from your father, which your father heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Ramadan and said: ""Ramadan is a month whose fasting Allah has obligated, and I have established for the Muslims its standing in prayer. Whoever fasts it and stands it in prayer emerges from sin as on the day his mother bore him."""
"866","Bishr ibn al-Walid, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri and Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us; they said: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Majishun informed us, from Salih ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: I was standing on the day of Badr in the row, looking to my right and left, when I found myself between two young boys of the Ansar. I wished I were between sturdier men than them. Then one of them nudged me and said: O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl? He said: I said: Yes; and what need have you of him, O son of my brother? He said: I have been told that he reviles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I saw him, my form would not part from his form until the sooner of us dies. He said: So I marvelled at that; then the other nudged me and said the like to me. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people, and I said to them: Do you not see? This is your man whom you ask about. So they rushed at him and struck him with their two swords until they killed him. Then they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: ""Which of you killed him?"" Each one of them said: I killed him. He said: ""Have you wiped your two swords?"" They said: No. So he looked at the two swords and said: Both of you killed him. Then he awarded his spoil to Mu'adh ibn 'Amr ibn al-Jamuh; and the name of the other was Mu'adh ibn 'Afra'."
"867","Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Basri narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrating from his father, from his grandfather 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Quraysh, the Ansar, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, Ashja' and Sulaym are my allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."" 'Amr ibn Yahya said: So I met Ishaq ibn Sa'd in the mosque and said to him: My father narrated to me from your father; so I narrated the hadith to him, and he said: They are only seven; I do not know which one is missing. 'Amr said: And my father mentioned from another besides him that the one missing among them is Sulaym."
"868","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, a man of the people of Ta'if narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Shurahbil, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer: for Allah said: {And after the night prayer, three times of privacy for you}; and the Bedouins call it al-'Atamah — while al-'atamah is the camels at milking time."""
"869","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Hammad, from 'Amr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, he said: I entered the mosque and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming out of the mosque. I followed him, walking behind him while he was unaware of me, until he entered a palm grove, faced the qiblah and prostrated, prolonging the prostration while I was behind him, until I thought Allah had taken his soul. So I came walking until I reached him, lowered my head to look at his face, and he raised his head and said: ""What is with you, O 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf?"" I said: When you prolonged the prostration, I thought Allah had taken your soul, so I came to look. He said: ""When you saw me enter the palm grove, I met Jibril, and he said: I give you glad tidings that Allah says: Whoever greets you with peace, I grant him peace; and whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him."""
"870","From the Musnad of Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, from Abu 'Ubaydah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This affair will remain established upon justice until a man of Banu Umayyah breaches it."""
"871","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Al-Awza'i, from Makhul, from Abu Ubaydah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The affair of my Ummah will remain established with justice until the first one to breach it will be a man from Banu Umayyah called Yazid."""
"872","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, Sa'd ibn Samurah ibn Jundub narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: The last words spoken by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were: He said: ""Expel the Jews of the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who take their graves as mosques."""
"873","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani who said: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Mu'adh ibn Jabal were conversing privately with each other, so I said to them: Have you not preserved the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding me. And he had entrusted them with me. They said: We did not intend to hold a private conversation excluding you; we were only recalling a hadith the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, and they began reminding each other of it. They said: This matter began as prophethood and mercy, then there will be caliphate and mercy, then there will be biting kingship, then there will be arrogance and tyranny and corruption in the Ummah, making silk and wine and private parts (unlawful intercourse) lawful, and corruption in the Ummah; they will be given victory for that and will be provided sustenance forever until they meet Allah."
"874","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, al-Anmati narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, with its isnad, and he mentioned something similar."
"875","Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""There was no prophet after Nuh except that he warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described him to us and said: ""Perhaps some of those who have seen me or heard my speech will encounter him."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our hearts be on that day, like they are today? He said: ""Or better."""
"876","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maslamah, that a man from the Muslims granted protection to a man from the polytheists, so Khalid ibn al-Walid and Amr said: Do not grant protection. Abu Ubaydah said: Grant him protection; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some of the Muslims grant protection on behalf of all the Muslims."
"877","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maslamah who said: A man granted protection to some people while he was with Khalid ibn al-Walid, Abu Ubaydah, and Amr ibn al-As. Khalid and Amr said: We will not honor the protection of one he granted protection to. Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some of the Muslims grant protection on behalf of all the Muslims."
"878","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma', the nephew of Juwayriyah, narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Wasil, the freed slave of Abu Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Sayf al-Jarmi, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, a man from the jurists of the people of Syria, from Iyad ibn Utayf who said: I entered upon Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah during his illness while his wife Tuhayfah was sitting at his head, and he had turned his face toward the wall. I said: How did Abu Ubaydah spend the night? She said: He spent the night with reward. He said: By Allah, I did not spend the night with reward. He said: It was as if the people were displeased, so he said: Will you not ask me about what I said? They said: What you said did not please us, so how should we ask you? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the path of Allah, it is multiplied seven hundredfold, and whoever spends upon his family, or visits a sick person, or removes a harm, then a good deed is worth ten like it, and fasting is a shield so long as one does not tear it, and whomever Allah afflicts with an affliction in his body, it is an expiation for him."
"879","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah and Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, they said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Salih ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah saying: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ordered twelve young she-camels for us, and we were in the process of taking them out when his death came, so people prevented us from them until they gathered. He said: So I said to Abu Juhayfah: Narrate to me about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He was a white man whose temples had turned gray."
"880","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, you have turned gray? He said: ""Hud and its sisters have turned me gray."""
"881","Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me awake; indeed Satan cannot take my form."""
"882","Isma'il ibn Musa al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Umar, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah saying: Good fortune (ancestral glory/wealth) was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer. One man said: The good fortune of so-and-so is in horses, another said: The good fortune of so-and-so is in camels, another said: The good fortune of so-and-so is in sheep, and another said: The good fortune of so-and-so is in slaves. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he raised his head from the last rak'ah and said: ""O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything after that,"" until he reached: ""And the good fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."" He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prolonged his voice on the word fortune, so that they would know it is not as they say."
"883","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Juhayfah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Describe him to me. He said: White, and he had turned gray."
"884","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to a man with him: ""I do not eat reclining."""
"885","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the one among people who most resembled him was al-Hasan ibn Ali."
"886","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer on Friday. An old man said to him: ""By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, and I never saw him do as you do."" He said: When I heard him mentioning from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: How did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I saw him come out when the sun had declined, and behold the old man was Abu Juhayfah."
"887","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to us, from his father who said: ""I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah while he was at al-Abtah in a red tent of his made of leather. He said: Bilal came out with his ablution water, some obtaining and some sprinkling. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in a red garment, as if I am looking at the whiteness of his legs. He said: He performed ablution and Bilal called the adhan. He said: I began following here and there, saying: right and left, saying: Come to prayer, come to success. Then a short spear was fixed for him, and he stood and prayed Asr two rak'ahs, then a donkey and a dog would pass in front of him without being prevented, then he continued praying two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah."""
"888","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I do not eat reclining."""
"889","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar who said: I heard Abu Juhayfah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I do not eat reclining."""
"890","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that he bought a slave boy who was a cupper, and he ordered his cupping instruments to be broken. I said to him: Are you breaking them? He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood and the price of a dog and the earnings of a prostitute, and he cursed the tattooing woman and the woman who seeks tattooing, and the eater of usury and the one who feeds it, and he cursed the image-maker."""
"891","Abu Khaythamah said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, that he heard Abu Juhayfah narrating ""that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution at midday heat, and people began taking from the leftover of his ablution, then he prayed Zuhr two rak'ahs and Asr two rak'ahs, with a short spear in front of him."""
"892","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something similar, with the addition: ""A donkey and a woman pass behind it."""
"893","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, ""that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward a short spear."""
"894","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father who said: ""We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah at al-Abtah, and he said: 'Welcome, you are from me.' When the time of prayer came, Bilal came out and called the adhan, placing his fingers in his ears and turning during his adhan. When the iqamah was said, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed a spear and prayed toward it."""
"895","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his journey in which they slept until the sun rose, and he said: 'You were dead, then Allah returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps past a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes, and whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers.'"""
"896","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas who said: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the price of blood, and the dowry of a prostitute."""
"897","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that a man slaughtered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the Day of Sacrifice, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It does not suffice for you."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadha'ah (young goat)? He said: ""It will suffice for you, but it will not suffice for anyone after you."""
"898","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Abu Umays narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda'. He said: Salman came visiting Abu al-Darda' and saw Umm al-Darda' in shabby clothes. He said: What is the matter with you? She said: Your brother has no need of this world. When Abu al-Darda' came, Salman welcomed him and brought food near to him. Salman said to him: Eat. He said: I am fasting. Then he said: I swear to you that you must eat; I will not eat until you eat. He said: So he ate with him and spent the night with him. When part of the night passed, Abu al-Darda' stood up, and Salman made him sit down, then he said: O Abu al-Darda', your Lord has a right over you, your family has a right over you, and your body has a right over you. Give everyone with a right his right: fast and break fast, stand (in prayer) and sleep, and come to your wife. When it was near dawn he said: Stand now. They stood and prayed, then went out to the prayer. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, Abu al-Darda' stood to him and informed him of what Salman had said, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him the like of what Salman had said to him."
"899","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim and al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfah who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this part of him was white - meaning his tuft below the lower lip."" It was said to him: Like whom were you at that time? He said: I used to sharpen arrows and feather them."
"900","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, Umarah ibn Thawban narrated to us, that Abu al-Tufayl informed him: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Ji'ranah distributing meat, while I was at that time a boy carrying a camel limb. He said: A Bedouin woman came forward, and when she drew near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he spread out his cloak for her and she sat upon it. I asked: Who is she? They said: His mother who nursed him."""
"901","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed me, from Abu al-Tufayl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened (ramal) from one stone to the other."
"902","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, he sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Nakhlah, where al-Uzza was. Khalid ibn al-Walid came to it, and it was upon the hills of acacia trees; he cut the acacias and demolished the house that was over it, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: ""Go back, for you have done nothing."" Khalid returned, and when the custodians - its doorkeepers - saw him, they went deep into the mountain, saying: O Uzza, afflict him with madness, O Uzza, blind him, or else die in disgrace. He said: Khalid came to it, and behold a naked woman with her hair spread, throwing dust upon her head. He struck her head with the sword until he killed her, then returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: ""That was al-Uzza."""
"903","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated to us, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl ibn Wathilah who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House upon his camel, touching the Stone with a staff he had with him."""
"904","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Habib and Humayd, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""While I was drawing water tonight, black sheep and dusty-white sheep came upon me. Abu Bakr came and drew one or two bucketfuls in which there was weakness, and Allah forgives him. Then Umar came and it turned into a large bucket, filling the basins and watering those who came. I never saw a strong gifted man among people drawing better than him. I interpreted the black sheep as the Arabs and the dusty-white ones as the non-Arabs."""
"905","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Unays, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: ""It has reached me that Ibn Sufyan ibn Nubayh al-Hudhali has gathered people against me to attack me, and he is at Nakhlah or Uranah, so go to him."" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me so I may recognize him. He said: ""The sign between you and him is that when you see him you will feel a shudder."" He said: So I went out wearing my sword until I came upon him among women in litters, seeking a dwelling place for them, at the time of Asr. When I saw him I felt what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had described to me of the shudder. I headed toward him, fearing there might be a struggle between me and him that would distract me from the prayer, so I prayed while walking toward him, gesturing with my head. When I reached him he said: From where is the man? I said: A man from the Arabs who heard of you and your gathering against this man, and came for that. He said: Yes, indeed I am engaged in that. He said: I walked with him a while until when I was able, I struck him with the sword until I killed him. Then I left, leaving his womenfolk bent over him. When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me, he said: ""The face has prospered."" He said: I said: I killed him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""You have spoken the truth."" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with me and admitted me into his house and gave me a staff, saying: ""Keep this staff with you, O Abdullah ibn Unays."" He said: I went out with it to the people, and they said: What is this staff? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to me and commanded me to keep it. They said: Why do you not go back and ask him why that is? He said: I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this staff? He said: ""A sign between me and you on the Day of Resurrection; indeed the fewest people on that day will be those holding short staffs."" Abdullah joined it to his sword, and it remained with him until when he died he ordered it to be placed with him in his shroud, then they were buried together, may Allah have mercy on him."
"906","Al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Unays narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Yazid, my uncle, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Unays, ""that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him alone on a military expedition."""
"907","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' al-Ansari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, my mother's father, from Abdullah ibn Unays who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Abu Qatadah, and an ally of theirs from the Ansar, and Abdullah ibn Atik, to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq to kill him. We went out and came to Khaybar at night. We traced their doors and locked them upon them from outside, then gathered the keys and threw them away. The people climbed into the palm trees, and I and Abdullah ibn Atik entered the stairway of Abu al-Huqayq. Abdullah ibn Atik spoke, and Ibn Abi al-Huqayq said: May your mother be bereaved of you, Abdullah, how did you come to this town? Get up and open, for a generous man is not turned away from his door at this hour. She got up, and I said to Abdullah ibn Atik: Go ahead. He brandished the sword over them, and his wife went to scream, so I brandished (the sword) at her, then remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade killing women and children, so I held back. Abdullah ibn Unays said: I entered upon him in his upper chamber, and stood looking at his intense whiteness in the darkness of the house. When he saw me he took a pillow and shielded himself with it. I went to raise the sword to strike him but could not because the house was low, so I stabbed him with a thrust, then left. My companion said: Did you do it? I said: Yes. He entered and stood over him, then we came down the stairs. Abdullah ibn Atik fell on the stairs and said: O my leg, my leg is broken. I said to him: There is nothing wrong with your leg. I put down my bow and carried him - and Abdullah was short and slight - so I brought him down and behold his leg was fine. We went until we joined our companions, and the woman screamed: O a night attack! The people of Khaybar rose up. Then I remembered the place of my bow on the stairs, and said: By Allah, I will surely return and take my bow. My companions said: The people of Khaybar have risen; you will be killed? I said: I will not return until I take my bow. I returned and behold the people of Khaybar had risen, and their only talk was: Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq? I would not look at anyone's face nor would anyone look at mine except I said as they said: Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq? Until I came to the stairs and climbed with the people, took my bow, then joined my companions. We would travel by night and hide by day; when we hid by day we would appoint a watcher to look out for us, until when we neared Madinah, at al-Bayda', I was their watcher. Then I waved to them with my garment, and they descended and came out running, and I descended after them and caught up with them until we reached Madinah. My companions said to me: Did you see anything? I said: No, but I saw the hardship that had reached you, so I wanted fear (of pursuit) to carry you along. We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing the people, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The faces have prospered."" We said: May your face prosper, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""So you killed him?"" We said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the sword with which he was killed, and said: ""This is his food (trace) on the edge of the sword."""
"908","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Iyad informed me, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abu al-Qasim Miqsam, the freed slave of Banu Rabi'ah, from al-Harith who said: I prayed in the mosque of Banu Ghifar, and when I sat I began supplicating and pointing with one finger. Khufaf ibn Ima' al-Ghifari entered upon me while I was like that, and said: What do you mean by this when you point with one finger? He said: I said: I supplicate Allah and ask Him. He said: Well done, indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that. The polytheists said: He only casts magic with it. The polytheists lied; that is only sincerity (toward Allah)."
"909","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Muhammad informed me, from Khalid ibn Abdullah ibn Harmalah, from al-Harith ibn Khufaf, that he said: Khufaf ibn Ima' said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, then raised his head and said: ""Ghifar, may Allah forgive it; Aslam, may Allah grant it peace; and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan, and curse Ri'l and Dhakwan."" Then he fell prostrate. Khufaf said: The cursing of the disbelievers was made for that reason."
"910","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah, from his father Uqbah, the freed slave of Jabr ibn Atik al-Ansari, who said: I witnessed Uhud with my master, and I struck a man from the polytheists. When I killed him I said: Take it from me, and I am the Persian man. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Why did he not say: Take it, and I am the Ansari man? For the freed slave of a people is from themselves."""
"911","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Sayyar narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid al-Qasri upon the pulpit saying: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Yazid ibn Asad, love for people what you love for yourself."""
"912","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Yahya ibn Amr ibn Salamah al-Hamdani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Qays ibn Malik al-Arhabi: ""In Your name, O Allah, from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah to Qays ibn Malik: peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings and His forgiveness. To proceed: I have appointed you over your people: their Bedouins and their villagers, their freed slaves and their entourage, and I have granted you from the wheat of Yasar two hundred sa', and from the raisins of Khaywan two hundred sa', that shall remain current for you and your descendants after you forever and ever."" Qays said: And the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""forever and ever"" is more beloved to me; I hope my descendants will remain forever. Yahya said: Their urb (Bedouins) means the people of the desert, and their khumur (villagers) means the people of the towns."
"913","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, my brother al-Miswar ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah, from his father Abdullah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions, he said: ""May Allah send blessings upon that graveyard"" three times. He said: We did not know which graveyard, and he did not name anything to them. He said: One of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah entered upon one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Attaf said: I was told it was A'ishah - and said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the people of a graveyard and invoked blessings upon them, but did not tell us which graveyard it is. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her and she asked him about it, and he said to her: ""The people of a graveyard in Asqalan."""
"914","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Buhaynah who said: The iqamah for prayer was called, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man praying two rak'ahs before Fajr, and he spoke to him something we do not know what it was. When we finished we surrounded him asking him: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: ""He said to me: One of you is about to pray Fajr as four rak'ahs."""
"915","Abu Salamah ibn al-Sabbak narrated to us, Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out for the Fajr prayer while a man was praying, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his shoulder and said: ""Do you intend to pray four? Or twice?"""
"916","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abu Kurayb narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ubayd ibn Salman al-Qurashi, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Jahjah al-Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believer eats with one intestine, and the disbeliever eats with seven intestines."""
"917","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something similar."
"918","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Ash'ath, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from al-Jarud al-Abdi who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, and I said to him: If I leave my religion and enter your religion, will Allah not punish me in the Hereafter? He said: ""Yes."""
"919","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The lost property of a Muslim is the kindling of the Fire."""
"920","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sallam ibn Amr, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Your brothers - treat them well - or he said: set right your conduct toward them - seek their help in what overcomes you, and help them in what overcomes them."""
"921","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, that Lahi'ah ibn Uqbah narrated to him, from Amr ibn Rabi'ah, from Salamah ibn Qaysar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hell like the distance of a crow that flew as a chick until it died of old age."""
"922","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Amrah, from his father who said: ""We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), four men, with a horse with us. He gave each one of us a share, and gave the horse two shares."""
"923","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid, from his father, from his grandfather, who had companionship, that he went out visiting one of his brothers but did not reach him until it reached him that he was sick. When he entered upon him he said: I came to you as a visitor, or I came to you as one visiting the sick, or as a bearer of glad tidings. He said: How have you combined all of this? He said: I went out intending to visit you, but I did not reach you until your complaint reached me, so it became a sick-visit, and I give you glad tidings of something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a station with Allah has gone ahead for a servant which his deeds do not reach, He afflicts him in his body, or in his wealth, or in his child, then grants him patience until he attains the station that went ahead for him from Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"924","Abu Talib narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ajlan al-Ansari, that Abu Kathir al-Muharibi narrated to him, that Kharashah narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him, he said: There will be tribulations after me; the one sleeping in them is better than the one awake, the one sitting in them is better than the one standing, and the one standing in them is better than the one walking. Whoever they come upon, let him take his sword, then walk to a rock and strike it until it breaks, then lie down for it until it passes as it passes."
"925","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Khalid ibn Adi al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking and without aspiring to it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only a provision Allah has driven to him."""
"926","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd who said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrating from a man of his people called Abu Malik or Ibn Malik, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever takes an orphan among Muslims into his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes certainly due for him; and whoever reaches his parents or one of them, then does not honor them, then enters the Fire, Allah will distance him; and whichever Muslim frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire."""
"927","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Malih, from Abu Azzah - a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends to take a servant's soul in a land, He makes for him a need in it."""
"928","Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Qurran ibn Tamam narrated to us, from Ayman ibn Nabil al-Makki, from Qudamah ibn Abdullah who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his camel, touching the Stone with his staff."""
"929","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ibn Sinan - meaning Burd, if Allah wills - from Utbah ibn Ali, from Yahya ibn Zayd, from Abu Unaysah, from Abu Layla who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and we went out with him. He passed by a man from Banu Adi uncovering his thigh, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for the thigh is part of the private area."""
"930","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Qays ibn Muslim, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to me, that his father informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep, appointing for every ten of his Companions a sheep."
"931","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah al-Juhani who said: We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we camped in a land with many lizards. We caught them, and the pots were boiling with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is this?"" We said: Lizards we caught. He said: ""A nation from Banu Isra'il was transformed, and I fear these may be them."" So he commanded us and we overturned them while we were hungry."
"932","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with something like a shield in his hand. He placed it, then urinated toward it. One of the people said: Look at him urinating as a woman urinates. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him and said: ""Woe to you, do you not know what befell the man of Banu Isra'il? When anything of urine touched them they would cut it with scissors, so he forbade them and was punished in his grave."""
"933","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Maysarah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a food-seller selling his food, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O owner of the food, is the bottom of the food like its top?"" He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever cheats the Muslims is not from them."""
"934","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far, from Rafi' ibn Bashir al-Sulami, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A fire is about to come out from Habs (a place), moving like slow camels move: traveling by day and hiding by night, going in the morning and evening. It will be said: The fire has gone in the morning, O people, so go in the morning; the fire has said midday, O people, so rest at midday; the fire has gone in the evening, O people, so go in the evening. Whomever it overtakes, it will consume him."""
"935","Abu Abdullah ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, al-Talqani Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid standing in the market looking at people passing."
"936","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""I am riding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not greet them first with peace, and when they greet you, say: And upon you."""
"937","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his uncle Yazid ibn Thabit who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to al-Baqi', and he saw a fresh grave. He said: ""What grave is this?"" They said: So-and-so, the freed woman of so-and-so, died at midday while you were napping, so we disliked waking you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and arranged us behind him, and said takbir over her four times, then said: ""No one should die while I am among you except that you inform me."" He said: And I think he said: ""For my prayer for him is a mercy."""
"938","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah, from his father, ""that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage (nikah al-mut'ah)."""
"939","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah, from his father Sabrah ibn Ma'bad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""Enjoy yourselves with these women."" He said: And enjoyment with us means marriage. He said: We offered that to the women, but they refused unless they fixed a term between us and them. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Do so."" So I and a cousin of mine went out, each of us having a cloak. He said: We passed by a woman, and my youth pleased her, as did my cousin's cloak. She said: A cloak like a cloak. So I married her, and slept with her that night. Then in the morning I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between the Door and the Corner, saying: ""I had permitted you temporary marriage, so whoever has any of them with him, let him separate from her, for Allah has forbidden it until the Day of Resurrection."""
"940","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in camel resting-places, and permitted praying in sheep folds."
"941","And from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""An arrow suffices a man as a screen in prayer; when one of you prays, let him screen himself even with an arrow."""
"942","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Attar Ishaq ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sari' who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every child is born upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses for him; then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian."""
"943","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah narrated to us, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes lawful with a dirham in marriage has made lawful."""
"944","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Raja' ibn Abi Salamah, from Sulayman ibn Musa who said: Malik ibn Abdullah al-Khath'ami passed while he was over the people in the summer campaign in the land of Rome - and a man was leading his mount - and he said to him: Ride, for I see your mount is sturdy. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant's feet become dusty in the path of Allah except that Allah forbids the Fire upon them. He said: So Malik dismounted, and the people dismounted walking; no day was seen with more walkers than it."
"945","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Shafi' who said - and he was a physician - he said: Usayd ibn Hudayr called me and I cut for him the sciatic vein. He narrated to me two hadiths. He said: Two households of my people came to me: a household of Banu Zafar and a household of Banu Mu'awiyah. They said: Speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to apportion for us - or give us, or something like this. So I spoke to him, and he said: ""Yes, I will apportion half for each household of them; if Allah returns to us, we will return to them."" He said: I said: May Allah reward you with good, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""And you, may Allah reward you with good, for you - as far as I know you - are chaste and patient."" He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""You will encounter favoritism after me."" When Umar ibn al-Khattab distributed garments among the people, he sent me one of them; I deemed it small and gave it to my daughter. While I was praying, a young man from Quraysh passed by me wearing one of those garments, trailing it. I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""You will encounter favoritism after me."" I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. A man went to Umar and informed him. He came while I was praying and said: Pray, O Usayd. When I finished my prayer he said: What did you say? I informed him. He said: That was a garment I sent to so-and-so, and he is a Badri, Uhudi, Aqabi man; this youth came to him and bought it from him and wore it. Did you think that would happen in my time? I said: By Allah, O Commander of the Believers, I thought that would not happen in your time."
"946","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih - meaning Ibn Umar - narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Amir, from Urwah ibn Mudarris who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have exhausted (my mount). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever catches Jam' (Muzdalifah) and stands with the Imam until he departs has attained the Hajj; whoever does not catch Jam' has no Hajj."""
"947","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Amir who said: When Marwan fought al-Dahhak ibn Qays, he sent to Ayman ibn Khuraym al-Asadi and said: We would like you to fight with us. He said: My father and my uncle witnessed Badr and enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but Allah. If you bring me an exemption from the Fire, I will fight with you. He said: Go away, and he attacked him and reviled him. So Ayman began saying (verses)."
"948","Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned a tribulation and magnified it. He said: We said - or they said: O Messenger of Allah, if we live to see this, we will surely perish? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No, being killed will suffice you."" Sa'id said: I saw my brothers killed afterwards."
"949","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr, and whoever wrongfully takes anything of land will be encircled with it from seven earths."""
"950","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf who said: Arwa bint Aws came to us with a group of Quraysh, among them Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, and said: I would like you to come to Sa'id ibn Zayd and speak to him and remind him, for he has taken from my land into his land. So we stood and went to Sa'id until we came to him in his land at al-Aqiq. He came out to us and said: I know what brought you. Arwa bint Aws came to you and said: I take from her land into my land what is not mine. I will narrate to you what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes from land what is not his will be encircled with it to the seventh. And I heard him saying: Whoever fights defending his wealth and is killed is a martyr. He said: We said: By Allah, we will never speak to you about anything after this again. He said: And we mounted and left."
"951","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me, that his father narrated to him, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, that Arwa disputed with him over land. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be encircled with it from seven earths on the Day of Resurrection. Then he said: O Allah, if she is lying, blind her sight and make her grave in her house. He said: I saw her blind, feeling the walls, saying: The supplication of Sa'id ibn Zayd has struck me. While she was walking in the house, she fell into a well in the house and fell into it, and it became her grave."
"952","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land without right, he will be encircled with it from seven earths."""
"953","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning: ""Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will be encircled with it from seven earths, and whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."""
"954","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be encircled with it from seven earths on the Day of Resurrection."""
"955","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah who said: Marwan said to us: Go and reconcile between these two: Sa'id and Arwa. We came to Sa'id ibn Zayd, and he said: Do you think I took anything from her right? I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be encircled with it from seven earths; whoever takes charge of a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of Allah; and whoever cuts off his brother's wealth with his oath, Allah will not bless it for him."
"956","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl, he informed him that Sa'id ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever wrongfully takes anything of land will be encircled with it from seven earths."""
"957","Musa ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever revives a dead land, it is his, and an unjust root has no right."""
"958","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah who said: I asked Sa'd ibn Ibrahim about Banu Najiyah. He said: They are from us. Sa'd said: They narrate from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: They are a clan from me. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: And I am from them."
"959","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, al-Ala' informed me, from Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever unjustly cuts off a handspan of land, Allah will encircle him with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."""
"960","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Yukhannis, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of al-Hasan ibn Ali and said: ""O Allah, I love him, so love him."""
"961","Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shabib, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Truffles are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."""
"962","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Arwa bint Aws claimed against Sa'id ibn Zayd that he took something from her land, and she disputed with him before Marwan ibn al-Hakam. Sa'id said: Would I take anything from her land after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: And what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land will be encircled with it to seven earths. Marwan said to him: I will not ask you for proof after this. He said: O Allah, if she is lying, blind her sight and kill her in her land. He said: She did not die until her sight went, and while she was walking in her land she fell into a pit and died."
"963","Al-Himmani Yahya narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, ""that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi."""
"964","Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from a man, from Amr ibn Hurayth who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Zayd saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O assembly of Arabs, praise your Lord who has lifted the tithes from you."""
"965","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Truffles are from the manna which was sent down upon Banu Isra'il, and their water is a healing for the eye."""
"966","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna al-Nakha'i narrated to us, my grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah while he was in the mosque with the people of Kufah with him. Sa'id ibn Zayd came, and al-Mughirah made room for him and said: Here, sit. He seated him with him upon the couch. Sa'id ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Lying about me is not like lying about anyone; whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"967","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about truffles, and he said: They are from the manna, and their water is a healing for the eye."
"968","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Truffles are from the manna which was sent down upon Banu Isra'il, and their water is a healing for the eye."""
"969","Abu Khaythamah and Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim al-Mazini, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: I testify regarding nine that they are in Paradise, and if I testified regarding the tenth I would not sin. He said: It was said: How is that? He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hira', and he said: ""Be still, Hira', for there is upon you none but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr."" He said: It was said: Who are they? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, Uthman, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and Ibn Awf. He said: It was said: Who is the tenth? He said: I - meaning himself."
"970","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: We hid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) above Hira'. When we settled, it shook with us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with his hand then said: ""Be still, Hira', for there is upon you none but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr."" And upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'id ibn Zayd, who narrated the hadith."
"971","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah addressed us and spoke ill of Ali. Sa'id ibn Zayd stood and said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Prophet is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, Sa'd is in Paradise, and if I wished I could name the tenth."""
"972","Suwayd ibn Sa'id and Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, they said: al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: My father said, Abu Uthman narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Harithah and Sa'id ibn Zayd, that they both narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have not left after me among people a trial more harmful to men than women."""
"973","Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: I and Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Zayd ibn Amr, and he said: ""He will come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone."""
"974","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Amr heard Jabir narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""There will come upon people a time when a group of people go on campaign, and it will be said to them: Is there among you one who saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They will say: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then a group of people will go on campaign, and it will be said: Is there among you one who saw one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They will say: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then a group of people will go on campaign, and it will be said to them: Is there among you one who saw one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They will say: Yes, and victory will be granted to them."""
"975","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with a pebble, then forbade a man to spit in front of him or to his right, and said: ""Let him spit to his left, or under his left foot."""
"976","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata' ibn Yazid, from Abu Sa'id, ""that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales and two garments: the two garments being wrapping with the whole cloth (ishtimal al-samma') and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part, and (he forbade) touching (for sale) and throwing (for sale)."""
"977","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, who heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"978","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Bathing on Friday is obligatory upon every adult."""
"979","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, as a narration, he said: ""There is no charity in less than five awaq (of silver), there is no charity in less than five awsuq (of grain), and there is no charity in less than five dhawd (of camels)."""
"980","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Juhani narrated to me, from his father who said: I asked Abu Sa'id: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the lower garment? He said: Yes. I said: Narrate to me. He said: I heard him saying: The lower garment of the believer is to the middles of his shins; there is no harm for him in what is between that and the ankles, and what is below the ankles is in the Fire - three times - Allah does not look at one who drags his garment out of pride."
"981","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return."""
"982","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from his father - and his mother was with Abu Sa'id - he said: He said - meaning Abu Sa'id: O my son, when you are in the deserts, raise your voice with the adhan, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No jinn, human, stone, or tree hears his voice except that it will testify for him."
"983","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""It is about that the best wealth of a man will be sheep with which he follows the mountain peaks and the places of rain, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."""
"984","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, my father informed me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, said: ""No fire shall be lit at night."" Afterwards he said: ""Light fires and prepare food, for none after you will attain your mudd nor your sa'."""
"985","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Unays ibn Abi Yahya, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: A man from Banu Amr ibn Awf and a man from Banu Khudrah disputed about the mosque founded upon piety. The Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Umari said: It is the mosque of Quba'. He said: They went out until they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that. He said: ""It is this mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, and in that there is much good."""
"986","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, Sa'id ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""When a fly falls into the food of one of you, dip it, for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other is a cure."""
"987","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Awf, Abu al-Siddiq narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The Hour will not come until the earth is filled with injustice and enmity, then a man from my household - or he said: from my progeny - will come out and fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with injustice and enmity."""
"988","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing, or something like that."
"989","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, ""that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing."""
"990","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has little wealth, many dependents, good prayer, and does not backbite the Muslims, will come on the Day of Resurrection with me like these two."""
"991","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Qatadah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more shy than a virgin in her chamber."" And he said: The Hour will not come until the House is no longer pilgrimaged to."
"992","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the fetus of the she-camel and the cow, and he said: ""If you wish, eat it; its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."""
"993","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Iyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to like palm stalks, holding them in his hand. He entered the mosque one day with one of them in his hand, and saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque. He scraped them off with it until he cleaned them, then turned to the people angry and said: ""Would one of you like a man to face him and spit in his face? When one of you stands for prayer, he only faces his Lord, and the angel is to his right. So let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left or under his left foot. If haste overcomes him with sudden spittle, let him spit like this - and Yahya spat in his garment and folded part of it over part."""
"994","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Iyad informed us, from Abu Sa'id, that a man entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit. He called him and commanded him to pray two rak'ahs. Then he entered the mosque a second time while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit. He called him and commanded him to pray two rak'ahs. Then he said: ""Give charity."" So they gave charity, and he gave him two garments from what they gave. Then he said: ""Give charity."" So he cast off one of his two garments. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked what he did, and said: ""Look at this man: he entered the mosque in shabby appearance, and I hoped you would notice him and give charity to him or clothe him, but you did not. I said: Give charity, and they gave him two garments. Then I said: Give charity, and he cast off one of his garments. Take your garment."" And he rebuked him."
"995","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, Zaynab narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a man from the Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, what do we get for these illnesses that afflict us? He said: ""Expiations."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, even if little? He said: ""Even a thorn and what is above it."" He said: So he supplicated against himself that fever would not leave him until he dies, and would not keep him from Hajj, Umrah, jihad in the path of Allah, nor an obligatory prayer in congregation. No human touched his body except he felt its heat until he died."
"996","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bending the mouths of waterskins (to drink from them)."
"997","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Zaynab bint Ka'b narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, ""that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificial meat beyond three days, then permitted us to eat and store."" He said: Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man, the brother of Abu Sa'id, arrived, and they offered him dried sacrificial meat. He said: Is this from dried sacrificial meat? They said: Yes. He said: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it? Abu Sa'id said: Yes, but a new matter occurred in it: he had forbidden us to keep it beyond three days, and permitted us to eat and store."
"998","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Zaynab bint Ka'b narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, ""that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah: that its trees be cut or beaten (for leaves)."""
"999","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed various food of dates, and we traded it among ourselves with increase. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to sell it except measure for measure."""
"1000","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, advise me."" He said: ""Upon you is fear of Allah, for it is the gathering of all good; upon you is jihad, for it is the monasticism of the Muslims; upon you is remembrance of Allah and recitation of His Book, for it is a light for you on earth and a mention for you in heaven; and guard your tongue except for good, for thereby you overcome Satan."""
"1001","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Firas, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""A servant entered Paradise who never did any good at all. When death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter half of me in the sea and half of me on land. He commanded the sea and the land and they gathered him. He said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You. So He forgave him for that."""
"1002","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, something similar to this hadith; and the man was a grave-robber, so he was forgiven for his fear."
"1003","Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: I heard Talhah ibn Abdullah mentioning from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The highest of people in rank on the Day of Resurrection is the just ruler, and the lowest of people in rank on the Day of Resurrection is the ruler who is not just."""
"1004","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Three Allah will laugh to on the Day of Resurrection: the man when he stands at night praying, the people when they line up for prayer, and the people when they line up to fight the enemy."""
"1005","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks fast he rejoices, and when he meets Allah he rejoices. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."""
"1006","Abu Bakr and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord? He said: ""Do you suffer harm in seeing the sun at midday without clouds?"" He said: We said: No. He said: ""Do you suffer harm in seeing the moon on the night of full moon without clouds?"" He said: We said: No. He said: ""Then you will not suffer harm in seeing Him, just as you do not suffer harm in seeing them."""
"1007","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar."""
"1008","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abadah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The renegades (al-Mariqin) will be killed by the dearer of the two factions to Allah, and the nearer of the two factions to Allah."""
"1009","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Isma'il ibn Raja', from his father who said: Marwan brought out the pulpit and began the sermon before the prayer. A man stood and said: O Marwan, you have opposed the Sunnah: you brought out the pulpit when it was not brought out, and you began the sermon before the prayer. Abu Sa'id said: Who is this? They said: So-and-so. He said: As for this one, he has fulfilled what was upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees a wrong, let him change it with his hand; if he cannot, with his tongue; if he cannot, with his heart - and that is the weakest of faith."
"1010","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, that Abd al-Rahman narrated to him from his father Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""I have made sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah, as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred."" He said: Then Abu Sa'id would find one of us with a bird in his hand that he had caught, and would take it from his hand and release it."
"1011","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Maymun, from Ata' ibn Yazid, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees; and if he prays it in the open land, completing its ablution and its bowing and its prostration, his prayer reaches fifty degrees."""
"1012","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, from his paternal aunt, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman is married for one of three traits: for her wealth, for her beauty, for her religion. So upon you is the one with religion and character; may your right hand be dusted."""
"1013","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Atiyyah narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Among my Ummah is one who will intercede for a man and his household, and they will enter Paradise by his intercession."""
"1014","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Atiyyah narrated to me, that Abu Sa'id narrated to him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has been given his gift and hastened it, and I have stored my gift as intercession for my Ummah."""
"1015","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a sheep whose tail the wolf had cut off - may it be sacrificed with it? He said: ""Yes, sacrifice with it."""
"1016","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Asim say, and Sharhabil narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayra, Abu Sa'id, and Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gold for gold, and silver for silver, like for like, spot for spot, weight for weight; whoever gives extra or takes extra has dealt in riba."" Sharhabil said: ""If I did not hear it from them, may Allah admit me into the Fire."""
"1017","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""{Say: He is Allah, the One} equals one-third of the Qur'an."""
"1018","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to recite one-third of the Qur'an?"" That weighed heavily upon them, and they said: Who among us can bear that? He said: ""Let him recite {Say: He is Allah, the One}, for it equals one-third of the Qur'an."""
"1019","Shayban narrated to us, Ali ibn Ali al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim who supplicates to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, with a supplication except that He answers him, so long as it does not involve sin or severing ties of kinship — except that Allah grants him through it one of three traits: either He hastens his supplication for him, or He stores it for him in the Hereafter, or He averts from him an equivalent amount of evil."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, then we will supplicate abundantly? He said: ""Allah is more abundant."""
"1020","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade building over graves, or sitting upon them, or praying over them."""
"1021","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Atiyya ibn Sa'd, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am about to be called and I will answer, and I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between the heaven and the earth, and my kin, the people of my household. And the Subtle, the All-Aware has informed me that they will never separate until they return to me at the Hawd (Pool), so watch how you succeed me regarding them."""
"1022","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, Aflah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Sa'id, he said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn while he was distributing a distribution among the people, when a man from Banu Umayya stood up and said to him: Be just, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""I would be ruined and lost if I were not just; who will be just, woe to you?"" So Umar ibn al-Khattab sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to kill him, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am not one to kill my companions. There will emerge people who say the like of his words; they will recite the Qur'an and it will not pass beyond their throats; they will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots through the game. He took an arrow and looked at its binding and saw nothing in it, then looked at its head — meaning the shaft — and saw nothing in it, then looked at its feathers and saw nothing in it; it had outstripped the dung and the blood. Their mark is a man whose hand is like a woman's breast, like a piece of flesh that quivers, in which are hairs like the whiskers of a beast."" Abu Sa'id said: And I was present for this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and I was present with Ali on the day he killed them at Nahrawan. He said: Ali sought him but did not find him. He said: Then he found him after that beneath a wall with this description, so Ali said: Which of you knows this man? A man from the people said: We know him; this is Hurqus, and his mother is here. He said: So Ali sent for his mother and said to her: Who is this? She said: I do not know, O Commander of the Believers, except that I used to graze some sheep of mine in the days of ignorance at al-Rabadha, when something like a cloud came over me, so I conceived from it and gave birth to this one."""
"1023","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Maymun — who was a companion of al-Mu'tamir — narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: A young man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication through which I may attain good. He said to him: ""Come near."" So he drew near until his knee almost touched the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Say: O Allah, pardon me, for You are Pardoning, You love pardon, and You are Pardoning, Generous."""
"1024","Al-Hasan ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham Abu Kulayb, from Ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""He forbade the stud fee of the horse and the miller's fee (paid in flour)."""
"1025","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Atiyya narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed my private store to which I resort are my household, and my inner circle are the Ansar; so pardon their wrongdoers and accept from their righteous."""
"1026","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah will enter Paradise."""
"1027","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one of them greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between the heaven and the earth, and my kin, the people of my household; and they will never separate until they return to me at the Hawd (Pool)."""
"1028","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Atiyya narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed I have a Hawd (Pool) whose length is the distance between the Ka'ba and Bayt al-Maqdis, whiter than milk; its vessels are as many as the stars; and I am the prophet with the most followers on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1029","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sa'id, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the mosque founded upon piety, so he took a handful of pebbles, then struck the ground with them, then said: ""This"" — meaning the mosque of Madina."
"1030","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Utba, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This House will surely be pilgrimaged to, and umra will surely be performed to it, after the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj."""
"1031","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, in marfu' form: ""Indeed Allah says: A servant whose body I have kept sound and whose livelihood I have widened, yet five years pass over him without coming to Me as a pilgrim is surely deprived."""
"1032","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Mukhtar informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The child is the fruit of the heart, and he causes cowardice, miserliness, and grief."""
"1033","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, he heard Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""That a man killed ninety-nine people, then came asking: Is there repentance for him? So he came to a monk and asked him, and he said: There is no repentance for you, so he killed the monk. Then he kept asking, then he set out from one village to another village in which there were righteous people. He said: When he was partway along the road, death overtook him, so he inclined with his chest toward it, then died. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment gathered, and he was a handspan nearer to the righteous village, so he was placed among its people."""
"1034","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Fulan al-Ansari, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no sadaqa due on less than five awaq (of silver), nor on less than five dhawd (camels), nor on less than five awsuq (of grain); and the wasq is sixty sa's."""
"1035","Hudba narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""We went on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when sixteen days of Ramadan had passed; some of us fasted and some of us broke the fast, and neither did the fasting criticize the one who broke it, nor did the one who broke it criticize the fasting."""
"1036","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There will be two parties from my umma from which a renegade faction will emerge; the one of them closer to the truth will undertake killing them."""
"1037","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The wife of Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Safwan beats me when I recite, and he forbids me from fasting, and he does not pray until the sun has risen. So Safwan stood up and said: As for her saying he beats me — she recites my two suras (aloud and disturbs me); as for her saying he forbids me from fasting — I am a young man; and as for her saying he does not pray until the sun has risen — we are a household known for that; we do not wake until the sun has risen. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Do not fast except with his permission, and do not recite his sura."" And as for you, O Safwan, when you wake, then pray."""
"1038","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one has been given anything better than patience."""
"1039","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A wet dream, vomiting, and cupping do not break the fast of the fasting person."""
"1040","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people will come to Ibrahim, and they will say to him: Intercede for us with your Lord, and he will say: I told three lies."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is not one of them but that he used it as a plea in defense of Allah's religion: His saying: {He cast a glance at the stars, then said: Indeed I am sick}, and His saying: {Rather, the eldest of them did it}, and his saying to Sara: She is my sister."""
"1041","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk (intoxicants). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What did you drink?"" He said: I did not drink wine; they are only raisins and dates that I put in a gourd of mine. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins and dates together."
"1042","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi Hafsa, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""It is not lawful for anyone to be in a state of janaba in this mosque except you and me."""
"1043","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from al-Walid ibn Qays, that Abu Sa'id informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever combines in himself: fasting on Friday, visiting a sick person, attending a funeral, giving charity, and freeing a slave — Paradise becomes obligatory for him."""
"1044","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, and Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, from Bashir al-Khawlani, that al-Walid ibn Qays narrated to him that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Five acts — whoever does them in a day, Allah records him among the people of Paradise: whoever fasts on Friday, goes early to the Friday prayer, attends a funeral, and frees a slave."""
"1045","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was feverish, covered with a blanket, so he placed his hand upon him and felt its heat above the blanket. So Abu Sa'id said: How severe is your fever, O Messenger of Allah! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed that is how it is with us: trial is intensified upon us, and reward is multiplied for us."" We said: O Messenger of Allah, who among people faces the severest trial? He said: ""The prophets and the righteous. One of them would be tried with poverty until he found nothing but a cloak which he gathered around himself and wore, and he would be tried with lice until they killed him; and one of them would be more joyful at trial than one of you at a gift."""
"1046","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""The Lord will say on the Day of Resurrection: Today the people of the gathering will know who the people of generosity are? So it will be said: Who are the people of generosity, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The gatherings of remembrance (of Allah) in the mosques."""
"1047","Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Qatada, from Uqba ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There was a man among those before you who had never stored any good with Allah at all — Qatada explained it: he had never saved any good with Allah at all — he said to his sons at death: O my sons, what kind of father was I to you? They said: An excellent father. He said: When I die, burn me — or he said: grind me, or he said: violate (my body) — then when there is a fiercely windy day, scatter me. So he died and that was done to him. So Allah said: Be, and he was, quicker than the blink of an eye. So Allah said: O My servant, what carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O my Lord. So nothing prevented Him from forgiving him."" Salih ibn Hatim said: Mu'tamir said: My father said: I narrated this hadith to Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, so he said: Thus Salman narrated it to me, and he added in it: ""And scatter me in the sea."""
"1048","Abu al-Ash'ath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, and Asim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Ahwal narrated to us — and I copied it from Asim's copy — he said: Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, Qatada narrated to us, from Uqba ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man will take his father's hand on the Day of Resurrection and will cut through the Fire with him, wanting to admit him into Paradise. Then it will be announced that Paradise is not entered by a polytheist; indeed Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist. So he will say: O my Lord, my father. Then he will be transformed into an ugly form with a foul smell, and he will abandon him."" The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held that it was Ibrahim, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not add to them beyond that."
"1049","Ahmad, with the same chain, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus (azl). He said: ""Do you do that? It does not matter if you do not do it; there is no soul that Allah has decreed to exist except that it will exist."" Umar and Ibn Umar disliked azl, while Zayd and Ibn Mas'ud practiced azl."
"1050","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed when the believer desires a child in Paradise, its gestation, delivery, and youth will be as he desires, or the like thereof."""
"1051","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn al-Rabi', from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, he said: We were at the house of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Muhajirun and Ansar, when he came out to us and said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of you?"" They said: Yes. He said: ""The best of you are those who fulfill promises and are pleasant; indeed Allah loves the hidden, pious one."" He said: And Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by, so he said: ""The truth is with this one; the truth is with this one."""
"1052","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn al-Rabi', from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id — I think from his father, Abu Abd Allah doubted — he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was upon the wooden pulpit, saying: ""Little that suffices is better than much that distracts."""
"1053","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi', from Abu Salama, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When three go out on a journey, let one of them lead them in prayer."""
"1054","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his father, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty, and loves to see His blessing upon His servant."""
"1055","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: ""Indeed Allah is giving a concession — meaning regarding wine — so whoever has any of it, let him sell it and benefit from it."" We remained only a short while until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah has forbidden wine; so whoever is reached by this verse, let him neither sell nor drink."" He said: So the people turned to what they had of it and spilled it in the streets of Madina."
"1056","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, Sulayman al-Naji informed us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions when a man came, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will trade profitably with this one by praying with him?"" He said: So a man prayed with him."
"1057","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Qurayt, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan, observes its limits, and guards what he ought to guard of it, it expiates what came before it."""
"1058","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Firas, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever seeks repute, Allah will make his repute heard (in disgrace)."""
"1059","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no wudu for one who does not mention Allah's name over it."""
"1060","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Winter is the spring of the believer."""
"1061","With its chain he narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gatherings are of three kinds: safe, rewarded, and ruined."""
"1062","Muhammad ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted the minbar and said: ""O people, I had been shown Laylat al-Qadr, but it was taken away from me, and perhaps that is better; and I saw as though on my forearm were two bracelets of gold, so I disliked them and blew on them and they flew away, and I interpreted them as these two liars: the ruler of Yemen, whose name is al-Aswad ibn Ka'b al-Ansi, and the ruler of Yamama."" And al-Aswad had already spoken (claimed prophethood) in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1063","Shayban narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, Abu Nadra narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: While we were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came on his mount and began looking right and left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a surplus mount, let him give it to one who has no mount, and whoever has surplus provisions, let him give them to one who has no provisions."" Then he mentioned such kinds of wealth as he mentioned, until we thought that none of us had any right to any surplus."
"1064","From Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lagging among his companions, so he said to them: ""Come forward and follow me, and let those after you follow you; and people will keep lagging behind until Allah delays them, Mighty and Majestic."""
"1065","Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, that Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Muhammad, are you ill? He said: Yes. He said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqya upon you, from every disease that harms you, from every soul or envious eye; Allah cures you; in the name of Allah I perform ruqya upon you."""
"1066","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand by a wooden post, leaning upon it, delivering the sermon every Friday, until a man from the people came to him and said: If you wish, I will make for you something so that when you sit upon it, it is as though you are standing. He said: ""Yes."" So he made the minbar for him. When he sat upon it, the wooden post moaned like a camel moans over its young, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended and placed his hand upon it. The next day, I saw it had been moved. We said: What is this? They said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came last night, with Abu Bakr and Umar, and they moved it."
"1067","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: ""So the wooden post moaned like a milking camel moans."""
"1068","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Nasr, the flour merchant, narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'd al-Muzani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id saying: I saw in a dream as though I were beneath a tree, and as though the tree were reciting {Sad}. When it reached the prostration, it prostrated, and said in its prostration: ""O Allah, forgive me through it; O Allah, remove a burden from me through it, create gratitude in me through it, and accept it from me as You accepted the prostration of Your servant Dawud."" So I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: ""Did you prostrate, O Abu Sa'id?"" I said: No. He said: ""Then you have more right to prostration than the tree."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Sura Sad, then came to the prostration, and said in his prostration what the tree had said in its prostration."
"1069","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you strikes his servant and he mentions Allah, lift your hands."""
"1070","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umara, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no sadaqa on less than five awaq, nor on less than five awsuq, nor on less than five dhawd."""
"1071","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Sa'id, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and he passed by the village of Banu Salim and called out to a man — and he mentioned the hadith."
"1072","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad informed me, that Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir narrated to him, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Ali brought him a dinar he had found in the market, so he said: ""Announce it three times."" But he found no one who recognized it, so he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: ""Eat it"" — or: ""Do with it as you wish."" So he bought with it barley for three dirhams, dates for three dirhams, meat for a dirham, and oil for a dirham, and a dirham remained with him — and the exchange rate was eleven for a dinar — until later its owner came and recognized it, so Ali said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to eat it. So its owner went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned all that to him, and he said to Ali: ""Return it to the man."" He said: I have already eaten it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If something comes to us, we will pay it to you."""
"1073","Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiya al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There was no prophet but that he warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him. He is one-eyed, with a bulging pupil, unmistakable, as though it were phlegm on the side of a wall; his left eye is like a brilliant star. With him are the like of Paradise and Hell: his paradise is an eye full of smoke, and his fire is a green garden. Before him are two men warning the people of the villages; whenever they leave a village, its foremost enter it. He will overpower a man over whom none besides him is given power: he will slaughter him, then strike him with his staff, then say: Stand, then say to his companions: What do you think? Am I not your lord? And they will testify to him with shirk. Then the slaughtered man will say: O people, this is the false Messiah, the Dajjal, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of. Then he will return and slaughter him again, then strike him with his staff and say to him: Stand, then say to his companions: What do you think, am I not your lord? And they will testify to him with shirk. Then the slaughtered one will say: O people, indeed this is the false Messiah, the Dajjal, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of; this has only increased my insight about you. Then he will return and slaughter him a third time, strike him with his staff and say: Stand, then say to his companions: What do you think, am I not your lord? And they will testify to him with shirk. Then he will say: O people, indeed this is the false Messiah, the Dajjal, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of; this has only increased my insight about you. Then he will return and slaughter him a fourth time, but Allah will place a plate of copper upon his throat, so he will be unable to slaughter him."" Abu Sa'id said: By Allah, I had never seen copper except that day. He said: ""Then people will plant and sow after that."" Abu Sa'id said: We used to think that man was Umar ibn al-Khattab, because of what we knew of his strength and endurance."
"1074","I read this hadith to al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan, and he said: It is what I read to Sa'id ibn Khuthaym, from Fudayl, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: When this verse {And give the near of kin his due} was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Fatima and gave her Fadak."
"1075","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in the middle ten of Ramadan, seeking Laylat al-Qadr. Then he ordered the structure removed, so it was taken down; then it was shown to him in the last ten, so he ordered it restored. Then he came out to us and said: ""It has been shown to me, Laylat al-Qadr, and I came out to clarify it for you, but two men quarreled, so it was made forgotten to me. So seek it on the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth."" I said: O Abu Sa'id, you know counting better than we do, so which nights are the ninth, seventh, and fifth? He said: Yes, and we have more right to that: when it is the night of the twenty-first, then leave a night, then the one that follows is the third; then leave the night, and the one that follows is the fifth. Al-Jurayri said: Abu al-Ala' narrated to me, from Mutarrif, that he heard Mu'awiya saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And the third."""
"1076","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The key of prayer is wudu, its sanctity begins with the takbir, its release is the taslim; in every two rak'as there is a taslim; and no prayer is valid in which al-Fatiha and something with it are not recited."""
"1077","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra — I think from Abu Sa'id — that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people of Madina, do not eat the meat of sacrifices beyond three days."" He said: So they complained to him that they had dependents and servants, so he said: ""Eat, feed, and store."""
"1078","And from Abu Nadra — I think from Abu Sa'id — that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he put on a garment, named it by its name — a turban, a shirt, or a cloak — and said: ""O Allah, to You is praise; You clothed me; I ask You its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for."""
"1079","And from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a river of water while he was on a mule and the people were fasting, with many on foot, and said: ""Drink."" But they kept looking at him, so he said: ""Drink, for I am the least burdened among you."" But they kept looking at him, so he shifted his thigh and drank, and the people drank."
"1080","And from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and noticed phlegm in the qibla of the mosque, so he scraped it with a stick he had, or a reed. Then he turned to the people, with anger recognizable on his face, and said: ""Who is the owner of this?"" The people fell silent, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Would any one of you, when he stands in his place of prayer, like a man to face him and spit in his face?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we would not like that. He said: ""Then Allah is before you, so let none of you confront with any filth what is before him; rather to his left or beneath his foot."""
"1081","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he put on a new garment, named it by its name. He said: O Allah, You clothed me with this shirt, or cloak, or turban; we ask You its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for."""
"1082","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ruined are the wealthy, ruined are the wealthy, except — "" They said: O Messenger of Allah, except whom? He said: ""Except one who says thus and thus, to his right and to his left (spending in charity)."""
"1083","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""How can I enjoy comfort when the bearer of the Trumpet has taken it up, bent his forehead, waiting for when he will be ordered to blow?"" It was said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say that day? He said: ""Say: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs; upon Allah we rely."""
"1084","Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah gave the Qur'an and he recites it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, so he says: If I were given the like of what this one was given, I would do as he does; and a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it in its right, so he says: If I were given the like of what this one was given, I would do as he does."""
"1085","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Isma'il ibn Raja', from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Among you is one who will fight over the interpretation of the Qur'an as I fought over its revelation."" So Abu Bakr said: Am I he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No. Umar said: Am I he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""No, but it is the one mending the sandal"" — and he had given Ali his sandal to mend."
"1086","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhada narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile my companions; for if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, you would not reach the mudd (measure) of one of them, nor half of it."""
"1087","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust imam (ruler)."""
"1088","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Tuwala, from Nahar al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The servant will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked: What prevented you, when you saw the evil, from denouncing it? Then if Allah inspires His servant with his proof, he will say: O my Lord, I hoped in You and feared people."""
"1089","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-A'mash, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Umm Salama, praying in a single garment wrapped around himself."
"1090","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubayda narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No nation is sanctified in which the weak is not given his right without being shaken off."""
"1091","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Ansar are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment; and were it not for the Hijra, I would be a man of the Ansar."""
"1092","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Jahdam ibn Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying what is in the bellies of livestock until they give birth, and what is in their udders except by measure, and buying a runaway slave, and buying spoils of war until they are divided, and buying charity until it is received, and the diver's strike (buying what a diver brings up unseen)."
"1093","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Firas, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an when he enters Paradise: Recite and ascend. So he will recite and ascend a degree with every verse."""
"1094","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Iyad, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""We used to make him inherit in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"" — meaning the grandfather."
"1095","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Umara ibn Ghaziyya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Umara, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying ones with: There is no god but Allah."""
"1096","Al-Abbas narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Maslama narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: ""The people of the Fire who are its (eternal) people — they neither die nor live; but there are people — or as he said — whom the Fire afflicts for their sins — or he said: for their faults — this is how Abu Nadra said it — so it kills them until they become charcoal, then permission is given for intercession, so they are brought in bundles and scattered upon the rivers of Paradise. Then it is said to the people of Paradise: Pour upon them. So they grow as a seed grows in the flood-borne silt."" A man from the people said: It is as though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the desert. Isma'il said: Al-hibba is the seed that falls from the tree and dung befalls it, so it grows; thus the Arabs name it."
"1097","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah's mercy is one hundred parts; He divided one part among creation; in it they show mercy to one another: people, beasts, and birds."""
"1098","Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Abbas: ""O boy, O little boy — or: O little boy, O boy — memorize from me words..."" then he mentioned the hadith in al-Mu'jam."
"1099","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'ara narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ghusl on Friday is obligatory upon every Muslim, and touching perfume if he has it."""
"1100","Hudba narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered to us a sermon after the Asr prayer until sunset; whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""To proceed: This world is sweet and green, and Allah is making you stewards in it and watching how you act. So beware of this world and beware of women. Indeed every treacherous one will have a banner according to his treachery, and there is no treachery greater than the treachery of a leader of a community. Indeed the best of men is one slow to anger and quick to return, and the worst of men is one quick to anger and slow to return; if one is quick to anger and quick to return, it balances out, and if one is slow to anger and slow to return, it balances out. Indeed the best of merchants is one good in settling debts and good in seeking them, and the worst of merchants is one bad in settling and bad in seeking; if a man is bad in settling but good in seeking, it balances out, and if a man is good in settling but bad in seeking, it balances out. Indeed anger is a coal kindled in the belly of the son of Adam; have you not seen his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins? So whoever senses any of that, let him cling to the ground. And let not fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he knows it. Indeed the best jihad is a word of truth before an unjust ruler."" When it was near sunset, he said: ""Indeed the measure of this world that has passed, in what remains of it, is like the measure of this day of ours that has passed, in what remains of it."""
"1101","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best rows of men are the frontmost, and the worst of them are the rearmost; and the best rows of women are the rearmost, and the worst of them are the frontmost."""
"1102","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, he said: A man took his wife on his camel (for intercourse from behind) in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: So-and-so took his wife on his camel, so Allah revealed: {Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish}."
"1103","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim al-Balkhi narrated to us, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b asking Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id: What did you hear from your father narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The example of one who plays with dice then stands to pray is like one who performs wudu with the pus and blood of a pig, saying: His prayer is not accepted."""
"1104","Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar Abu Ayyub narrated to us, Sahl ibn Amir narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be, at the end of time, amidst prolonged life and a break in time, an imam who will be the most generous of people; a man will come to him and he will scoop for him into his lap; his concern will be who will accept that wealth's charity from him, between him and his family, because of the good that befalls people."""
"1105","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Sulayman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The example of the believer and the example of faith is like a horse at its tether: it roams then returns to its tether; and the believer errs, then returns to faith. So feed your food to the pious, and direct your kindness to the believers."""
"1106","Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Dahhak, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and al-A'mash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ibn Abi Layla; and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to recite one-third of the Qur'an in a night?"" They said: Who can bear that? He said: ""Let him recite: {Say: He is Allah, the One}, for it is one-third of the Qur'an."""
"1107","Ishaq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ali ibn Ali al-Rifa'i narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, opened his prayer with the takbir, then said: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You,' three times; 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great,' three times; 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry, and his pride.' Then he recited."""
"1108","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever humbles himself for Allah by a degree, Allah raises him a degree, until He places him in Illiyyin; and whoever is arrogant toward Allah by a degree, Allah lowers him a degree, until He places him in the lowest of the low."""
"1109","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will mention a people in this world upon well-spread beds, and Allah will admit them into the highest degrees."""
"1110","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Ubayda narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Jarud, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim who feeds a Muslim out of hunger except that Allah feeds him from the fruits of Paradise; no Muslim who clothes his brother out of nakedness except that Allah clothes him from the green garments of Paradise; and whoever gives a Muslim drink out of thirst, Allah gives him drink from the sealed nectar."""
"1111","Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man wakes in the night and prays two rak'as, he is recorded among those who remember Allah much, men and women."""
"1112","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Hakam ibn Abd Allah al-Qass narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1113","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, from his father, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps through the witr or forgets it, let him pray the witr when he wakes or remembers it."""
"1114","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Raqaba, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayra, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will come upon people a time when foolish rulers will rule over you; they will advance the worst of people, suppress their best, and delay prayer from its times. So whoever among you reaches that, let him not be a headman, nor a policeman, nor a tax collector, nor a treasurer."""
"1115","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata' ibn Yazid, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales and two garments: as for the two sales, mulamasa and munabadha; and as for the two garments, wrapping in a single garment (ishtimal al-samma'), and he forbade sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing between him and the sky covering his private part."
"1116","Ishaq narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, from Yahya ibn Umara, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying ones with: There is no god but Allah."""
"1117","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun, he said: We said to Abu Sa'id: Did you memorize anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say after giving salam? He said: Yes, he used to say: {Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."
"1118","Ishaq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Abu Isa, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Visit the sick, and follow funerals; they remind you of the Hereafter."""
"1119","Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said regarding: {When the matter is decreed while they are in heedlessness}, he said: ""In this world."""
"1120","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Damra ibn Sa'id, if Allah wills: I heard from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, saying: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr and after Fajr."""
"1121","Ishaq narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah."""
"1122","Ishaq narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment wrapped around himself."""
"1123","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouths of waterskins."
"1124","Ishaq narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The key of prayer is wudu, its sanctity begins with the takbir, and its release is the taslim."""
"1125","Ishaq narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur ibn Zadham narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr. We estimated his standing in Zuhr, in the first two rak'as, at about thirty verses per rak'a, the length of the recitation of (Tanzil — al-Sajda). We estimated his standing in the first two rak'as of Asr at the length of the last two of Zuhr, and we estimated his standing — meaning in the last two — at half of that."""
"1126","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, conveying from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Ghusl on Friday is obligatory upon every adult."""
"1127","Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Adi ibn Abi Umara narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There will surely rise over my umma, from my household, one with a narrow (high) forehead and receding hairline; he will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice and tyranny; he will rule seven years."""
"1128","Asim ibn al-Nadr al-Ahwal narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Qatada narrated to us, from Hilal, brother of Banu Murra ibn Abbad, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Abu Sa'id said: ""We suffered severe want, so my family ordered me to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for something. So I set out, and the first thing I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying was: 'Whoever seeks richness, Allah will enrich him; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; and whoever asks us, we will not withhold from him anything if we find it' — or as he said. So I said to myself: I shall seek richness and Allah will enrich me; I shall keep chaste and Allah will keep me chaste. So I did not ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anything."""
"1129","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir ibn Qarawanda narrated to us, he said: I heard Atiyya al-Awfi saying: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The people of the highest degrees will surely be seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star rising on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."""
"1130","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir ibn Qarawanda narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, he said: I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about Allah's saying: {Indeed He who imposed the Qur'an upon you will surely return you to a place of return}, he said: ""His return is his Hereafter."""
"1131","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered fasting Ashura, though he himself did not fast it."
"1132","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal (continuous fasting). Abu Sa'id said: ""So this sister of mine fasts continuously, and I forbid her, but she refuses."""
"1133","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id, and from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice, and prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets. Abu Harun said: Abu Sa'id said: ""Fast thereafter as you wish, and pray thereafter as you wish."""
"1134","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Qaza'a, from Abu Sa'id, he said: Azl was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Do you practice it? — and he did not say: Do not practice it — There is no soul that Allah creates except that Allah is its Creator."""
"1135","Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let no man look at the nakedness of another man, nor a woman look at the nakedness of another woman; and let no man lie with another man in a single garment, nor a woman lie with another woman in a single garment."""
"1136","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Dimashqi, from Qaza'a, from Abu Sa'id, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after ruku': 'O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and the earths, and filling whatever You will after that; none can withhold what You give; the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You; the best a servant has said — truly, all of us are servants to You; none can withhold what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You.'"""
"1137","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""A neck will emerge from Hell on the Day of Resurrection, saying: I have charge of three: every obstinate tyrant, whoever sets up another god with Allah, and whoever kills a soul without (right of) a soul."""
"1138","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not mix unripe dates and ripe dates (for nabidh)."""
"1139","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""O people, I had left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray after me: the two weighty things, one of them greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended from the heaven to the earth, and my kin, the people of my household; and they will never separate until they return to me at the Hawd (Pool)."""
"1140","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibn Abi Kathir, from Iyad, he said: I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, saying: One of us prays and does not know how much he prayed? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: ""When one of you prays and does not know how much he prayed, let him prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting. Then if Satan comes to one of you and says: You have passed wind, let him say: You lie — unless he finds a smell or hears a sound with his ear."""
"1141","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I forbid you fasting two days: al-Fitr and al-Adha."""
"1142","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Utba, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like thereof."
"1143","Uqba narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ya'juj and Ma'juj will emerge, emerging as Allah said: {From every mound they hasten}. They will flood the earth, and the Muslims will withdraw from them until the remnant of the Muslims are in their cities and fortresses, gathering their cattle to themselves. Their vanguard will pass by a river and drink it until they leave nothing in it; then their rearguard will pass after them and one of them will say: There was once water here. Then they will prevail over the earth, and one of them will say: These people of the earth — we are done with them; let us contend with the people of heaven — until one of them shakes his spear then hurls it toward the sky, and it returns stained with blood. So they will say: We have killed the people of heaven. While they are thus, He will send upon them creatures like the grubs of locusts, seizing them by their necks, and they will die the death of locusts, piled upon one another. The Muslims will wake and hear no sound of them, so they will say: Who will sell his soul to see what they have done? A man among them, having resigned himself to being killed by them, will find them dead, and call to them: Rejoice! Allah has destroyed your enemy. So the people will come out and release their cattle, whose only pasture will be their flesh; and they will thrive upon them as well as they ever thrived upon any vegetation."""
"1144","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughira ibn Mu'ayqib, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Utwar who was an orphan under Abu Sa'id's care, from Abu Sa'id, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""When Allah gathers people on a single plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will advance, part of it riding upon part, its keepers restraining it. It will say: By my Lord's might, either I shall be left with my spouses, or I shall overwhelm people all at once. They will say: Who are your spouses? It will say: Every arrogant tyrant. So it will thrust out its tongue and snatch them with it from among the people, hurling them into its belly. Then it will withdraw. Then it will advance, part of it riding upon part, its keepers restraining it. It will say: By my Lord's might, either I shall be left with my spouses, or I shall overwhelm people all at once. They will say: Who are your spouses? It will say: Every tyrannical ingrate. So it will snatch them with its tongue from among the people and hurl them into its belly. Then it will withdraw. Then it will advance, part of it riding upon part, its keepers restraining it. It will say: By my Lord's might, either I shall be left with my spouses, or I shall overwhelm people all at once. They will say: Who are your spouses? It will say: Every conceited boaster. So it will snatch them with its tongue from among the people and hurl them into its belly. Then it will withdraw, and Allah will judge between the servants."""
"1145","Uqba narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, with a tongue that speaks, saying: I have been entrusted today with three: whoever sets up another god with Allah, every obstinate tyrant — and he did not name the third — so it will fold over them and cast them into the depths of Hell."""
"1146","Uqba narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughira, from Sulayman ibn Amr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise was shown to me, and I went to take a cluster from it to show you, but I was prevented from it."" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how big is a berry of its grapes? He said: ""Like the greatest bucket your mother ever emptied."""
"1147","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: ""We took captives on the day of Awtas who had husbands, and we disliked falling upon them, so we asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was revealed: {And married women, except what your right hands possess} — so we deemed them lawful."""
"1148","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Na'ama, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed in his sandals."
"1149","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi asking Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id: What did you hear from your father narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The example of one who plays with dice..."" and he mentioned the hadith."
"1150","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from al-Ala' ibn Bashir — he was, as far as I knew, brave in battle and weeping at remembrance — from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Abu Sa'id said: I was among a group of weak Muhajirun; some of them would shield themselves with others from nakedness. A reciter of ours would recite to us, and we would listen to the Book of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood over us; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over us, the reciter fell silent. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What were you doing?"" We said: O Messenger of Allah, a reciter was reciting and we were listening to the Book of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Praise be to Allah, who placed in my umma those with whom I was commanded to be patient."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in our midst to make himself equal among us. Then he gestured with his hand: Form a circle, so the circle turned and their faces appeared to him. I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recognize any of them but me. Then he said: ""Rejoice, O company of poor Muhajirun, of enduring light on the Day of Resurrection: you will enter Paradise before the rich believers by half a day, and that is five hundred years."""
"1151","Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Atiyya, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the sons of al-Hakam reach thirty, they will take Allah's religion as a mere claim, Allah's servants as slaves, and Allah's wealth as something to pass around."""
"1152","Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We took women on the day of Hunayn and practiced azl with them, so some of us said to others: You do this while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is among you? So we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Not all fluid produces a child; when Allah wills to create something, nothing can prevent Him."""
"1153","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from his brother Ma'bad ibn Sirin, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""It does not matter if you do not do it, for it is but decreed."""
"1154","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us; Unays ibn Abi Yahya said: He informed us, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us in the illness in which he died, his head bandaged. I followed him until he stood upon the minbar, and said: ""I am now standing over the Hawd (Pool)."" Then he said: ""A servant was offered the world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter."" None of the people understood it but Abu Bakr, who said: With my father and mother for you — rather we would ransom you with our wealth, our souls, and our children. Then he descended from the minbar, and was not seen upon it again until that hour (of his death)."
"1155","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Utba saying: I heard Abu Sa'id saying: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber; and when he disliked something, we recognized it in his face."""
"1156","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you see the funeral bier, stand; and whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is placed down."""
"1157","And from Abu Salama, he said: We discussed Laylat al-Qadr among a group of Quraysh, so I went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who was a friend of mine, and said: Will you not go out to the palm groves? So he went out wearing a khamisa (cloak). I said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Yes. We observed i'tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle ten of Ramadan; we came out on the morning of the twentieth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: ""I saw Laylat al-Qadr, but I was made to forget it — or: it was made forgotten to me — so seek it in the last ten, in every odd night. And I saw myself prostrating in water and mud. So whoever observed i'tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him return."" So we returned, seeing no wisp of cloud in the sky; then a cloud came and we were rained upon until the mosque flowed — and it was of palm stalks — the prayer was established, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in water and mud, till I saw the trace of mud on his forehead."
"1158","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you follow a funeral, do not sit until it is placed down."" Suhayl said: I saw Abu Salih not sitting until it was lowered from the shoulders of the men."
"1159","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Qaza'a, from Abu Sa'id, he said: I heard something from him that pleased me, so I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Would I attribute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I did not hear? He said: I heard him saying: ""Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque."" He said: And I heard him saying: ""A woman shall not travel two days of time except with her husband or a mahram of hers."" He said: And I heard him saying: ""Prayer is not valid after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, nor after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."" And I heard him saying: ""Fasting is not valid on two days: the day of Fitr from Ramadan, and the day of Adha."""
"1160","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umara ibn Umayr, from Qaza'a, he said: The saying of A'isha to Abu Sa'id was mentioned: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'as after Asr. He said: He says: As for me, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""No prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor after Fajr until the sun rises."""
"1161","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Sa'id - or from Ibn Abi Sa'id - from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters."""
"1162","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Sa'id, who said: 'Ali sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen gold in tanned, dyed leather that had not been purified, and he divided it among four men: Zayd al-Khayl, al-Aqra' ibn Habis, 'Uyaynah ibn Hisn, and 'Alqamah ibn 'Ulathah. Some people among the Muhajirun and the Ansar said: We were more deserving of this. That reached him and it distressed him, and he said: ""Do you not trust me when I am the trustee of the One in heaven? News of heaven comes to me morning and evening?"" Then a man with protruding eyes, prominent cheeks, a jutting forehead, a thick beard, a shaven head, and a tucked-up waist-wrapper stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, fear Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to you, am I not the most deserving person on earth of fearing Allah?"" Then he turned away, and Khalid, the sword of Allah, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck? He said: ""No; perhaps he prays."" He said: If he prays he says with his tongue what is not in his heart. He said: ""I was not commanded to split open the hearts of people, nor to split open their bellies."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him as he was turning away and said: ""From the stock of this man there will emerge a people who recite the Book of Allah but it does not pass their throats; they shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the game."" 'Umarah said: I think he said: ""If I were to reach them I would kill them as Thamud were killed."""
"1163","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning one who has intercourse and then wants to repeat it: let him perform ablution."
"1164","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qaza'ah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade farewell to a man and said to him: Where do you intend to go? He said: I intend Bayt al-Maqdis. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in my mosque is better than a hundred elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."""
"1165","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qaza'ah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no fasting on a day of festival, and a woman may not travel three days except with a mahram."""
"1166","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of Madinah, and al-Aqsa Mosque."""
"1167","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No child of adultery shall enter Paradise, nor a habitual drinker of wine, nor one undutiful to his parents, nor a giver of reminders of his favours."""
"1168","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and Fatimah is the mistress of the women of Paradise, except for what was of Maryam daughter of 'Imran."""
"1169","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A pilgrim in ihram may kill the black snake, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the little vermin."" He said: I said: What is the little vermin? He said: The mouse. I said: And what is the matter of the mouse? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up when it had taken the wick and climbed with it to the ceiling."
"1170","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: There was something between Khalid ibn al-Walid and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, and Khalid reviled him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile any of my Companions, for if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud, he would not reach the mudd of one of them nor half of it."""
"1171","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise and Hell disputed. Hell said: In me are the tyrants and the arrogant, and Paradise said: In me are the weak and poor among people. He said: Then He judged between them: You, Paradise, are My mercy; I show mercy through you to whom I will. And you, Hell, are My punishment; I punish through you whom I will. And upon Me is the filling of each of you."""
"1172","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Nuh will be called on the Day of Resurrection and will say: At Your service and at Your happiness, O Lord. He will say: Did you convey? He will say: Lord, yes. He will say to his nation: Did he convey to you? They will say: No warner came to us. It will be said: Who testifies for you? He will say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his nation. He said: Then they will testify that he conveyed, and the Messenger will be a witness over you. That is His saying: {We made you a middle nation that you may be witnesses over people}. He said: And 'middle' means just."""
"1173","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal beats me when I pray, makes me break my fast when I fast, and does not pray the dawn prayer until the sun has risen - and Safwan was with him. He asked him about what she said, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, as for her saying that he beats me when I pray, she recites two surahs though I forbade her from them. He said: ""If it were a single surah it would suffice people."" He said: As for her saying that he makes me break my fast when I fast, she goes and fasts while I am a young man and cannot restrain myself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: ""No woman shall fast except with her husband's permission."" As for her saying that he does not pray until the sun has risen: we are a household in whom that is known; we hardly wake until the sun has risen. He said: ""When you wake, then pray."""
"1174","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, it will be said: O people of Paradise. They will crane their necks and look. Death will be brought like a white-and-black-spotted ram, and it will be said to them: Do you recognize this death? They will say: It is this, and all of them will have recognized it. It will be brought forward and slaughtered. Then it will be said to them: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death. And O people of Hell, eternity with no death. He said: That is His saying: {And warn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter is decided while they are in heedlessness and they do not believe}."""
"1175","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Arta'ah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and ripe dates."""
"1176","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins and dates."
"1177","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see the rising star on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."""
"1178","And with the same chain from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."""
"1179","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abi Muslim, narrating it from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and from Abu Hurayrah, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He grants respite until, when the first third of the night has gone, He - blessed and exalted - descends to the lowest heaven and says: Is there any seeker of forgiveness? Is there any asker? Is there any supplicant? - until dawn breaks."""
"1180","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Companions holding back, and said: ""Come forward and follow me, and let those behind you follow you; people will keep holding back from me until Allah puts them behind."""
"1181","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra' narrated to us, from 'Iyad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Sarh, from Abu Sa'id: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on the day of festival on his mount."""
"1182","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Jabr ibn Nawf Abi al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We took donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and the pots were boiling with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is this?"" We said: Donkeys we took. He said: ""Wild or domestic?"" We said: No, rather domestic. He said: ""Then overturn them."" He said: So we overturned them."
"1183","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of lizards, so what do you command us? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has reached me that a nation from the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts, and I do not know in which beasts - so he neither commanded us nor forbade us."""
"1184","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Sahba', from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Sa'id, raised to the Prophet, who said: ""In the morning the limbs atone for the tongue, saying: Fear Allah concerning us; if you are upright we are upright, and if you deviate we deviate."""
"1185","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the believers are saved from the Fire they will be detained at a bridge between Paradise and Hell, and they will settle with one another there wrongs that were between them in this world, until when they are cleansed and refined they will be permitted to enter Paradise. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, one of them knows his dwelling in Paradise better than you know the dwelling he lived in in this world."""
"1186","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be rulers over you surrounded by hangers-on from among people; whoever believes their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing - I am free of him and he is free of me. And whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing - he is of me and I am of him."""
"1187","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Aba Umamah ibn Sahl narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that Banu Qurayzah came down to the judgment of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, so a message was sent to Sa'd and he came on a donkey. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Stand for the best of you - or: for your chief. He said: These people have come down to your judgment."" He said: Then I judge concerning them that their fighters be killed and their offspring taken captive. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have judged with the judgment of Allah"" - and once he said: ""You have judged with the judgment of the King."""
"1188","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you hear the call, say the like of what the caller to prayer says."""
"1189","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from 'Amir - Abu Khaythamah said: al-Ahwal - from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning one who forgets a prayer: he prays it when he remembers it."
"1190","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah. Muzabanah is buying dates on the tops of palm trees, and muhaqalah is leasing land."""
"1191","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, Sayfi narrated to me, from al-Sa'ib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Madinah there is a group of jinn who have become Muslim; whoever sees anything of these house-snakes, let him warn it three times, and if it appears to him after that, let him kill it, for it is a devil."""
"1192","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ma'bad ibn Sirin, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""People will emerge from the east reciting the Qur'an, but it will not pass their collarbones; they will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the game, and they will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Their mark is shaving and close-cropping."""
"1193","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Na'amah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his sandals in prayer and placed them to his left, so they took off their sandals. He said: ""What is the matter with you?"" They said: We saw you take yours off so we took ours off. He said: ""Jibril came to me and informed me that there is filth in them. When one of you comes, let him look; if he sees filth or harm in them, let him wipe, then let him pray in them."""
"1194","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We had hardly passed Khaybar when we fell upon those greens - garlic and onions - and ate of them heavily. He said: And people were hungry. We returned to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found the smell and said: ""Whoever eats anything of these foul greens, let him not come near us in the mosque."" The people said: They are forbidden, they are forbidden. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""O people, it is not for me to forbid what Allah has made lawful, but it is a plant whose smell I dislike."""
"1195","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of sacrifices beyond three days."" He said: The people of Madinah complained to him that they had dependents. He said: ""Then eat, feed, and keep."" Al-Jurayri said: I do not know whether in this hadith or in another he said: ""And store."""
"1196","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a journey of three days or more except with her father, her son, her husband, or a mahram of hers."""
"1197","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile my Companions, for if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them nor half of it."""
"1198","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id or from Abu Hurayrah - al-A'mash doubted - who said: When the expedition of Tabuk came, the people were struck by hunger. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if you would permit us, we would slaughter our riding camels and eat and take oil. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""Do so."" 'Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, if they do that, mounts will become few; but call them with the surplus of their provisions, then supplicate for blessing over them - perhaps Allah will place blessing in that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a leather mat and spread it, then called for the surplus of their provisions. He said: A man would come with a handful of corn, another with a handful of dates, another with a piece of bread, until some of that gathered on the mat. He said: Then he supplicated for blessing over it, then said: ""Take in your vessels."" He said: They took in their vessels until they left no vessel in the camp but filled it. He said: And they ate until they were full. He said: And some remained over. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah; no servant meets Allah with them without doubting but he is screened from Paradise."""
"1199","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no charity in less than five awsaq."""
"1200","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no charity in less than five awsaq of dates or grain."""
